erware. With the purpose of fighting against technology facilitated abuse, the initiative aims to unite both organizations that work to combat domestic violence and the IT security community. https://stopstalkerware.org/',NULL,'2025-10-21 13:15:44'),(5036,'Geneva Dialogue on Responsible Behaviour in Cyberspace: The Geneva Dialogue is an international process established in 2018 to map the roles and responsibilities of non-state stakeholders – private sector, civil society, academia, and technical community – in contributing to greater security and stability in cyberspace. It is led by the Swiss Federal Department of Foreign Affairs (FDFA) and implemented by DiploFoundation, with support of the Republic and State of Geneva, C4DT, Swisscom and UBS. https://genevadialogue.ch/about/',NULL,'2025-10-21 13:15:44'),(5037,'IT-Sicherheitscluster: As an independent association, we are dedicated to shaping technological, political, and social developments in these areas, because we are firmly convinced that this task can only be mastered collectively. https://www.it-sicherheitscluster.de/english/',NULL,'2025-10-21 13:15:44'),(5038,'Cybermalveillance.gouv.fr: The mission of this private-public partnership initiative is to assist individuals, businesses, associations, communities and administrations who are victims of cybermalveillance, to raise their awareness of cyber risks, to inform them about digital threats and the means to protect themselves against them. https://www.cybermalveillance.gouv.fr/',NULL,'2025-10-21 13:15:44'),(5039,'Renaissance Numérique: an independent think-tank dedicated to the digital transformation of the society.',NULL,'2025-10-21 13:15:44'),(5040,'https://www.renaissancenumerique.org/',NULL,'2025-10-21 13:15:44'),(5041,'Interpol: Kaspersky contributes to the Gateway Project under the auspices of INTERPOL, sharing information, analyzing intelligence, and conducting and developing training.',NULL,'2025-10-21 13:15:44'),(5042,'https://www.interpol.int/es/P