s and new proposals','2025-10-21 12:41:11'),(321734,'RUDINE MM aligns with several key EU policies relevant to sustainable food production and agri-processing The company supports the Farm to Fork Strategy, promoting sustainable, local supply chains and food security Its investment in IQF processing and own dairy farm reflects alignment with the Common Agricultural Policy (CAP), particularly in improving agricultural resilience and value-added processing The company’s commitment to energy efficiency and reduced emissions aligns with the Renewable Energy Directive (RED II) and the Energy Efficiency Directive (EED) Furthermore, RUDINE MM supports the EU Green Deal goals, especially those related to circular economy principles in agri-food production and reducing food waste Through private-label export and regional cooperation, the company contributes to EU goals for rural development, innovation, and competitiveness in the food sector','2025-10-21 12:41:12'),(321735,'From Farm to Fork','2025-10-21 12:41:12'),(321736,'Trade Policy','2025-10-21 12:41:12'),(321737,'Market Access','2025-10-21 12:41:12'),(321738,'Corporate Reporting (Auditing, Accounting, Sustainability reporting)','2025-10-21 12:41:13'),(321739,'Corporate governance, economic governance, taxation (tax rulings, VAT, Head Office Tax System for SMEs, CCCTB)','2025-10-21 12:41:13'),(321740,'SMP professional qualifications/education and ethics','2025-10-21 12:41:13'),(321741,'SME affairs (SME access to finance, accounting and auditing and SME Relief Package)','2025-10-21 12:41:13'),(321742,'Policy proposals and connected legal and regulatory proposals on the digital future, digital economy, competition policy and regulations in relation to digital products and services, information-/cybersecurity and digital skills','2025-10-21 12:41:14'),(321743,'Groundhandling, Cargo handling, Freight handling, Self-handling, Airports, Aviation, Transport, Market access','2025-10-21 12:41:14'),(321744,'ICPAC is interested in actively participating in EU initiatives and discussions pertaining to: (a) the regulation of the audit profession, including matters of implementation specific legislative instruments such as Directive 2006/43/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 17 May 2006 on statutory audits of annual accounts and consolidated accounts and Regulation 537/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 16 April 2014 on specific requirements regarding the statutory audit of public interest entities, (b) the Directive 2013/34/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council of 26 June 2013 on the annual financial statements, consolidated financial statements and related reports and the application of the IFRS as approved by EU, (c) the prevention of the use of the financial system for the purposes of money laundering and/or terrorist financing, including matters of the implementation of specific legislative measures such as Directive (EU) 2018/843 of the European Union and of the Council of 30May 2018 amending Directive (EU) 2015/849, (d) the enrichment of personal data protection via legislative measures such as the General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679, (e) matters related to EU taxation policy and actions such as the implementation of Council Directive (EU) 2018/822 of 25 May 2018 amending Directive 2011/16/EU regarding mandatory automatic exchange of information in the field of taxation in relation to reportable cross border arrangements (f) matters relating to EU Foreign Investment Policy including Regulation (EU) 2019/452 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 19 March 2019 (g) matters relating to corporate and public governance and ethics, (h) contemporary matters of transformative effect including Brexit and the interaction thereof with legislative measures such as Directive 2005/36/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 7 September 2005 on the recognition of professional qualifications, Directive 2006/43/EC on statutory audits of annual accounts and consolidated accounts and the EU-UK Trade and Cooperation Agreement of 2020 regarding the recognition of regulated professions and professional qualifications, (i) company law matters, (j) competition law matters, as well as (k) matters relating to general accountancy practices','2025-10-21 12:41:15'),(321745,'ICPAC also intends to contribute in the discussion and consultation in the discourse related to Ethics, Compliance, Governance, Transparency and Anti-Corruption','2025-10-21 12:41:15'),(321746,'Ungt Säkerhetsforum följer främst EU:s gemensamma utrikes- och säkerhetspolitik (GUSP), cybersäkerhetsstrategin, ungdomsstrategin 2019–2027 samt initiativ kopplade till Youth, Peace and Security-agendan (YPS) Vi intresserar oss särskilt för strategier som rör ungas deltagande i säkerhetspolitiskt beslutsfattande, digital säkerhet, försvarssamarbete samt demokratifrämjande åtgärder i EU:s närområde','2025-10-21 12:41:16'),(321747,'Proposal for a Directive of the European Parliament and of the Council on improving working conditions in platform work (Platform Work Directive) Proposal for a Council Directive amending Directive 2006/112/EC as regards VAT rules for the digital age (VAT) Proposal for a Regulation of the European Parliament and of the Council laying down harmonised rules on Artificial Intelligence (Artificial Intelligence Act) Proposal for a Regulation of the European Parliament and of the Council on harmonised rules on fair access to and use of data (Data Act) Proposal for a Regulation of the European Parliament and of the Council on a Single Market For Digital Services (Digital Services Act) Notice on well-functioning and sustainable local passenger transport-on-demand (taxis and PHV) Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2017/1926 of 31 May 2017 supplementing Directive 2010/40/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council with regard to the provision of EU-wide multimodal travel information services Proposal for a Regulation of the European Parliament and of the Council addressing market challenges hampering the development of Multimodal Digital Mobility Services (MDMS) Transport data – creating a common European mobility data space Proposal for a Regulation of the European Parliament and of the Council on the deployment of alternative fuels infrastructure (AFIR) Proposal for a Regulation of the European Parliament and of the Council amending Regulation (EU) 2019/631 as regards strengthening the CO2 emission performance standards for new passenger cars and new light commercial vehicles in line with the Union’s increased climate ambition Proposal for a Directive of the European Parliament and of the Council on the framework for the deployment of Intelligent Transport Systems in the field of road transport and for interfaces with other modes of transport (ITS) Proposal for a Regulation of the European Parliament and of the Council on packaging and packaging waste, amending Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 and Directive (EU) 2019/904, and repealing Directive 94/62/EC (Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation)','2025-10-21 12:41:17'),(321748,'Öffentliche Konsultationen, Richtlinien, Verordnungen, Beschlüsse, Interinstitutionelle Vereinbarungen, Initiativberichte oder Entschließungen des Europäischen Parlaments','2025-10-21 12:41:22'),(321749,'Farm to Fork','2025-10-21 12:41:22'),(321750,'Renewable Energy','2025-10-21 12:41:22'),(321751,'Bioeconomy','2025-10-21 12:41:22'),(321752,'Contaminants and Residues in Food and Feed','2025-10-21 12:41:22'),(321753,'Food','2025-10-21 12:41:22'),(321754,'Feed','2025-10-21 12:41:22'),(321755,'Biofuels','2025-10-21 12:41:22'),(321756,'Food Information Labelling','2025-10-21 12:41:22'),(321757,'International Facility Management Association - Europe, Middle East and Africa is representing the Facility Management Professionals in the EMEA region On a European level we have been working on proposals to include FM related verbage in the texts of the Eneregy Perorm