-driven mental health solutions, safeguarding digital well-being, and preventing online harms','2025-10-21 12:42:04'),(321966,'European Education Area & Digital Education Action Plan (2021-2027) – Promoting inclusive education, mental health literacy, and youth resilience in digital learning environments','2025-10-21 12:42:04'),(321967,'MHR actively engages in consultations, policy discussions, and stakeholder collaborations to shape these legislative frameworks, ensuring a youth-centered and rights-based approach to mental health across the EU','2025-10-21 12:42:04'),(321968,'-EU Agenda on Migration','2025-10-21 12:42:05'),(321969,'-EU PACT on Asylum and Migration','2025-10-21 12:42:05'),(321970,'-EU Migration and Integration Pollicy','2025-10-21 12:42:05'),(321971,'-Negotiations on the EU Multi-Annual Financial Framework (MFF)','2025-10-21 12:42:05'),(321972,'Horizon Europe 2027 - 2034 legislation, European Competitiveness Fund legislation, ERA Act, Horizon Europe mid term evaluation, Digital Services Act, Artificial Intelligence Act, Multi-annual Financial Framework, DSM, Copyright legislation, Erasmus+ legislation','2025-10-21 12:42:06'),(321973,'Cohesion policy, Horizon Europe, Stability and Growth Pact, Recovery and Resilience Facility, Western Balkan Agenda on Innovation, Research, Education, Culture, Youth and Sport','2025-10-21 12:42:07'),(321974,'Areas of EU Health and Research are of particular interest to the EAPC include: management and treatment of all life-limiting conditions and chronic disease management across the lifespan Access to Healthcare Access to Medicines Innovative Treatments Quality of (Health)Care','2025-10-21 12:42:07'),(321975,'Specific legislative and related implementation acts that the EAPC follows include: EU4Health Horizon 2020, Horizon Europe and other research initiatives, Medicines Regulation (in particular related to access to controlled medication), Human Rights etc','2025-10-21 12:42:07'),(321976,'EAPC also follows EU initiatives in the following broad areas: Social Affairs, Skills and Education, Digital agenda, Mobility, Human Rights and Children’s Rights, Justice, Disability, Employment, Consumers etc','2025-10-21 12:42:07'),(321977,'The EAPC has, and continues to be involved in several European Union Funded research projects on palliative care  As well as producing well-utilised guidelines on cancer pain management in 2001 and reviewing and revising the guidelines in 2012, the EAPC was also a partner in the European Union funded project, ATOME (Access to opioid medication in Europe) This project investigated the reasons why opioid medication was inadequately used for moderate to severe pain in twelve European countries and provided evidence to support improved access to opioids The EAPC is also represented on the European Commission funded Civil Society Forum on Drugs Whilst much of the work of this group focuses on the tackling the issue of illicit use of drugs, the EAPC provides an expert voice on access to opioids for pain management for those requiring palliative care We are also currently lobbying to establish a Civil Society Forum on Palliative Care in order to advocate and lobby for access to and improvements in palliative care across Europe In 2019, the WHO withdrew two sets of guidelines on the use of opioids, one in children and the other in adults The EAPC was involved the establishment of new and updated guidelines','2025-10-21 12:42:07'),(321978,'Políticas e instrumentos de financiación de la Dirección General de Desarrollo y Cooperación de la Comisión Europea, especialmente, los relacionados con los Actores No Estatales y las Autoridades Locales','2025-10-21 12:42:08'),(321979,'REGULATION (EC) No 1905/2006 OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL (18/12/2006)','2025-10-21 12:42:08'),(321980,'Además, damos seguimiento al proceso legislativo de la Comisión de Desarrollo en el Parlamento Europeo','2025-10-21 12:42:08'),(321981,'Rail Passenger Rights','2025-10-21 12:42:08'),(321982,'Multi-modal passenger rights','2025-10-21 12:42:08'),(321983,'PSI Directive','2025-10-21 12:42:09'),(321984,'CRS Consultation','2025-10-21 12:42:09'),(321985,'Open Data Directive','2025-10-21 12:42:09'),(321986,'GDPR','2025-10-21 12:42:09'),(321987,'Travel Package Directive','2025-10-21 12:42:09'),(321988,'Pricing Transparency','2025-10-21 12:42:09'),(321989,'Consumer Directive','2025-10-21 12:42:09'),(321990,'PSD2','2025-10-21 12:42:09'),(321991,'Council Directive 92/43/EEC of 21 May 1992 on the conservation of natural habitats and of wild fauna and flora','2025-10-21 12:42:09'),(321992,'The European Green Deal','2025-10-21 12:42:09'),(321993,'Biodiversity strategy for 2030','2025-10-21 12:42:09'),(321994,'Die IHK Nord verfolgt europäische Initiativen zu ihren Schwerpunktbereichen Maritimes und Infrastruktur, Energie- und Industriepolitik, Tourismus, Ernährungswirtschaft und Außenwirtschaft, die für die gewerbliche Wirtschaft Norddeutschlands von Bedeutung sind Hinsichtlich des Schwerpunktthemas Maritimes und Infrastruktur liegen die Arbeitsschwerpunkte der IHK Nord in den Bereichen Schifffahrt und Logistik, maritime Infrastruktur sowie kohlenstoffarme Treibstoffe in der Schifffahrt und Landstrom Die IHK Nord verfolgt insbesondere die Einbeziehung des Seeverkehrs in den Europäischen Emissionshandel, die FuelEU Maritime Initiative zu kohlenstoffarmen Treibstoffen in der Schifffahrt sowie die Verordnung zu transeuropäischen Verkehrsnetzen (TEN-V) Bezüglich der Energie- und Industriepolitik verfolgt die IHK Nord die Themen Offshore Windenergie und Wasserstoff, konkret die europäische Offshore Strategie und die europäische Wasserstoffstrategie sowie verbundene Initiativen des Green Deal Im Bereich des Tourismus begleitet die IHK Nord europäische Initiativen mit Relevanz zum Tourismus an den norddeutschen Küsten, beispielsweise die Initiative zu kurzfristigen Vermietungen In der Ernährungswirtschaft liegt der Fokus auf den Themen Farm-to-Fork sowie Lebensmittelkennzeichnung, konkret die Themen geschützte geografische Angaben sowie Nutri-Score Der Arbeitsschwerpunkt Außenwirtschaft wird durch den Brexit sowie die Geoökonomie geprägt, darüber hinaus verfolgt die IHK Nord Initiativen im Bereich Zoll und Export','2025-10-21 12:42:10'),(321995,'For Arkos, as a modular construction company, some relevant EU policies and legislative proposals could include:','2025-10-21 12:42:11'),(321996,'EU Green Deal & Renovation Wave - Promoting modular, energy-efficient construction as part of sustainable building and renovation efforts across Europe','2025-10-21 12:42:11'),(321997,'Construction Products Regulation (CPR) – [Regulation (EU) 305/2011, ongoing revision] - Ensuring modular units meet harmonized technical standards for safety, sustainability, and CE marking','2025-10-21 12:42:11'),(321998,'Internal Market for Goods & Services - Supporting better market access for modular building exporters from Kosovo and the Western Balkans to the EU','2025-10-21 12:42:11'),(321999,'Single European Sky, Aviation package, Wise Persons Group Report, Airspace Architecture Study','2025-10-21 12:42:11'),(322000,'-EU Transport policies (Air, Sea, Land)','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322001,'-EU Energy policies','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322002,'-EU Digital policies','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322003,'Examples:','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322004,'-ReFuel EU Aviation,','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322005,'-FuelEU Maritime,','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322006,'-Emissions Trading System (ETS),','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322007,'-Renewable Energy Directive,','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322008,'-Net-Zero Industry Act,','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322009,'-Electricity Market Design (EMD),','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322010,'-Chemicals regulation such as CLP and REACH revision,','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322011,'-Ecolabel/Ecodesign,','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322012,'-Horizon Europe,','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322013,'-Sustainable Finance,','2025-10-21 12:42:12'),(322014,'-Raw Materials Act,'