,(322243,'1 Cyfrowa Dekada 2030','2025-10-21 12:43:00'),(322244,'2 Konkurencyjność Europy (Kompas) - implementacja wnioski z raportów Draghi i Letta','2025-10-21 12:43:00'),(322245,'3 EKŁE (Dyrektywa Parlamentu Europejskiego i Rady 2018/1972 z dnia 11 grudnia 2018)','2025-10-21 12:43:00'),(322246,'4 AI Act, GPAI code of practise','2025-10-21 12:43:00'),(322247,'revise OSH Framework Directive (89/391 EEC) and specifically in the 1989 Directive on workplace requirements (89/654/EEC)','2025-10-21 12:43:01'),(322248,'EU initiatives in the area of animal welfare, animal health, animal diversity, ethics, food security, research and development, technology development, transport, trade','2025-10-21 12:43:02'),(322249,'In particular EFEE follows EU initiatives in the field of Education and Training, Research, Social Affairs, Employment and Inclusion Key themes for EFEE are: Economic case for education and training Vocational education and training Citizenship and integration of migrants Open and innovative education Transition from education to employment Supporting early career researchers Healthy and save schools School leadership and self-evaluation','2025-10-21 12:43:02'),(322250,'In 2025, EFEE will on working, among others, on the following key themes:','2025-10-21 12:43:02'),(322251,'• promoting environmental sustainability   in   school   learning,   teaching   and   management','2025-10-21 12:43:02'),(322252,'•strengthening education employers’ capacity in order to promote innovation in education institutions in   a   post-Covid-19   era','2025-10-21 12:43:02'),(322253,'•addressing   psychosocial   risks   for   an   equitable  and sustainable education-led recovery from the COVID-19 pandemic','2025-10-21 12:43:02'),(322254,'Gebr Heinemann supports the European Travel Retail Confederation in working with Members of the European Parliament as well as Representatives of EU-Institutions on relevant Directives and Regulations that are of interest to the travel-retail industry This applies, for example, to EU Regulation No 1169/2011, where we have supported a uniform language for food labeling throughout the EU We are also following the developments of the VAT package for travel and tourism, possible amendments to the Tobacco Products Directive (2014/40/EU), particularly with regard to the impact on the travel-retail sector, as well as the introduction of national deposit return systems as part of the Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation (P9_TA(2024)0318) In general, we follow European transport policy, in particular sea and air transport issues, legislation relating to products sold in travel retail, customs and taxation, including travelers allowances, and other relevant legislation for the travel-retail market','2025-10-21 12:43:03'),(322255,'We follow legislative files and initiatives related to telecommunications, digital, data protection and data economy, cybersecurity and sustainability This includes, among others, the following legislative proposals: Digital Network Act, Omnibus Packages, Gigabit Infrastructure Act, Data Act, Digital Markets Act, AI Act, ePrivacy Regulation, e-evidence, GDPR, Cyber Resilience Act, Payment Service Regulation, EU Taxonomy, etc','2025-10-21 12:43:04'),(322256,'As a company headquartered in the UK and with a European-wide footprint serving businesses and governmental institutions with ICT solutions, we take a strong interest in the future EU-UK relationship','2025-10-21 12:43:04'),(322257,'Union of Skills','2025-10-21 12:43:07'),(322258,'Quality Jobs Roadmap','2025-10-21 12:43:07'),(322259,'Military Mobility','2025-10-21 12:43:07'),(322260,'Defence','2025-10-21 12:43:07'),(322261,'Energy Transition Partnership for EU Fisheries and Aquaculture','2025-10-21 12:43:07'),(322262,'European Industrial Maritime Strategy','2025-10-21 12:43:07'),(322263,'Sustainable Transport Investment Plan','2025-10-21 12:43:07'),(322264,'EU Competitiveness Fund','2025-10-21 12:43:07'),(322265,'EU Oceans Pact','202