nol, Amoniaco,):','2025-10-21 12:43:21'),(322355,'The European Green Deal, The Fit for 55 Package, Renewable Energy Directive (RED II), The Climate Law, The Innovation Fund, Horizon Europe, The Just Transition Mechanism, EU Strategy on Hydrogen, Sustainable Finance Disclosure Regulation (SFDR) or The Circular Economy Action Plan','2025-10-21 12:43:21'),(322356,'We are interested in all initiatives related to the social economy and social enterprises Both at a legislative level, as support initiatives and financing of these projects Finally, since we belong to a network of universities, we also have an interest in research projects related to the social economy','2025-10-21 12:43:21'),(322357,'We are interested in the following programmes:','2025-10-21 12:43:21'),(322358,'Social Business Iniciative (http://eceuropaeu/growth/sectors/social-economy/enterprises_en) H2020 programme EASI, Erasmus+ and COSME','2025-10-21 12:43:21'),(322359,'People involved in the Foundation\'s activities are co-authors of the EU Code of conduct on agricultural data sharing by contractual agreement We aim to influence EU policies or legislative proposals: adult learning, agriculture and rural development, better regulation, business and industry, competition, data protection, digital economy and society, education and training, the European market for space data, Information and Communication Technologies (ICT), investments in small business, skills and qualifications, vocational education and training, youth, youth employment, and entrepreneurship','2025-10-21 12:43:22'),(322360,'- EU:s ramdirektiv för vatten','2025-10-21 12:43:23'),(322361,'- EU:s gemensamma fiskeripolitik','2025-10-21 12:43:23'),(322362,'Rubber- en kunststofsector (verpakkingen industrieel, verpakkingen consument, consumentenproducten, bouw & constructie en B2B & Automotive), circulaire economie, Green Deal, Clean Sweep, MORE, inzet recyclaat','2025-10-21 12:43:23'),(322363,'Circulair economy package','2025-10-21 12:43:24'),(322364,'Waste legislation','2025-10-21 12:43:24'),(322365,'Waste Shipment Regulation','2025-10-21 12:43:24'),(322366,'End of Waste Status','2025-10-21 12:43:24'),(322367,'Energy- and Climate package','2025-10-21 12:43:24'),(322368,'Renewable Energy Directive','2025-10-21 12:43:24'),(322369,'REACh and links with recycling','2025-10-21 12:43:24'),(322370,'Substances of Very High Concern','2025-10-21 12:43:24'),(322371,'Plastic Strategy','2025-10-21 12:43:24'),(322372,'Extended Producers Responsibility','2025-10-21 12:43:24'),(322373,'BREFs','2025-10-21 12:43:24'),(322374,'As FDC exploits database rights, it is mainly interested in Database Directive and associated rights, including copyright protection for databases','2025-10-21 12:43:25'),(322375,'General Food and Food Safety Law','2025-10-21 12:43:26'),(322376,'Implementation of Food Information to Consumers','2025-10-21 12:43:26'),(322377,'Implementation of Common Agricultural Policy','2025-10-21 12:43:26'),(322378,'Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation','2025-10-21 12:43:26'),(322379,'Childhood Obesity Action Plan','2025-10-21 12:43:26'),(322380,'Nutrition and Health Claims','2025-10-21 12:43:26'),(322381,'Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive','2025-10-21 12:43:26'),(322382,'Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive','2025-10-21 12:43:26'),(322383,'Unfair Trading Practices','2025-10-21 12:43:26'),(322384,'Carbon Removal Certification Framework','2025-10-21 12:43:26'),(322385,'Emission Trading Scheme','2025-10-21 12:43:26'),(322386,'Based on our vast experience in Italian and EU cultural heritage regulation, we plan to contribute to the EU’s role to assist and complement the actions of Member States in preserving and promoting Europe\'s cultural heritage','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322387,'Our Association has been pursuing a dialogue with the Italian institutions aimed at facilitating the circulation of art (and, consequently of knowledge and culture) within the European territory','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322388,'For example, we have been in constant dialogue with the Italian parliament members and policy makers to assess whether the cumbersome and bureaucratic control exercised by the Italian export offices on the international circulation of art (into and out of the Italian territory) is the most efficient way to protect the European cultural heritage','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322389,'We believe that an over-protective and over-controlling system has the deterrent effect of preventing foreign and Italian collectors from shipping their artworks to Italy or making them publicly available with loans to public museums At the same time, also the fruition of Italian art by European citizens may be hindered due to a lengthy domestic export system guided by uncertain and overly discretional principles We would like to refer to our 2022 position paper  https://wwwgruppoapolloit/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/4_Apollo_position-paper_stampa_A4pdf','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322390,'We are planning to bring these issues to the attention of the European Institutions (EU Parliament and Commission) also in light of the Council Resolution on the Workplan for Culture 2023/2026 (2022/C 466/01)','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322391,'In particular, we believe that a better circulation of art within Europe is consistent with the following Guiding Principles (Annex I) of the above-mentioned Resolution:','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322392,'-	Culture, including cultural heritage, has an intrinsic value and contributes to strengthening European identity','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322393,'-	Cultural and linguistic diversity are fundamental assets of the EU and are to be respected, promoted and enhanced, including through mobility and the circulation of works (emphasys added)','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322394,'-	Freedom of artistic expression and creativity are fundamental to the human ability to address challenges, to think critically, to innovate and to invent, and they must be encouraged and supported in all relevant ways','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322395,'-	Cultural diversity and intercultural dialogue are essential for the promotion and protection of human rights they foster mutual understanding, help prevent and resolve conflicts and promote reconciliation, peace and international stability, and any misuse of culture with the aim of spreading war propaganda and disinformation and of instigating hatred is incompatible with the fundamental values and principles of the EU','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322396,'-	Culture makes a significant contribution to sustainable development, the economy and social inclusion, enhancing territorial cohesion','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322397,'-	Culture has the potential to promote equality and mutual respect, and to fight against all forms of violence, discrimination, intolerance and prejudice','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322398,'Propuestas legislativas o políticas de la UE relacionadas con los objetivos de nuestra institución, entre otros I+D+i (Programa Horizonte Europa, Life, RFCS, Interreg) y educación superior (Erasmus+) En concreto, políticas relacionadas con las prioridades del entorno regional, como la política de transición justa, descarbonización, pacto verde, economía circular, digitalización, etc','2025-10-21 12:43:28'),(322399,'Ibex Publishing\'s strategic communications consultancy services are designed to provide advisory support to corporate entities and non-corporate clients regarding optimal engagement strategies with governmental and public institutions on matters of policy, legislation, and regulation pertinent to their interests The specific European Union legislative proposals and/or policies under scrutiny are subject to the particular interests of our clientele however, they encompass initiatives such as ReFuelEU Aviation, FuelEU Maritime, the EU Emissions Trading Scheme (ETS), the trans-European transport network (TEN-T), and CO2 emission performance standards for cars and vans','2025-10-21 12:43:29'),(322400,'Clean Sky','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322401,'SESAR','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322402,'EASA','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322403,'Aviation package','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322404,'Energy Union','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322405,'Strategic Transport Research and Innovation Agenda','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322406,'Clean Aviation','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322407,'Single European Sky ATM Research','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322408,'SBA','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322409,'Technology Infrastructures','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322410,'Drone Strategy','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322411,'RefuelEU','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322412,'EDF','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322413,'Sustainable and Smart Mobility Strategy','2025-10-21 12:43:30'),(322414,'Areas:','2025-10-21 12:43:31'),(322415,'Drinking water, water, waste water, chemicals, circular economy, climate mitigation and adaptation, research, taxonomy, crisis management, renewable energy, critical infrastructure','2025-10-21 12:43:31'),(322416,'Keywords:','2025-10-21 12:43:31'),(322417,'- Crisis handling, risk management and security • Supply chain challenges, lack of chemicals, spare parts and other resources, electrical power failures and shutdowns • Lessons learnt from utility management during the Covid-19-pandemic','2025-10-21 12:43:31'),(322418,'– Climate change adaptation and resilience • Climate change mitigation • Sustainable stormwater management • Energy efficiency, Energy strategies and priorities • Greenhouse gas emissions and climate ambitions • Biogas production, upgrading and use','2025-10-21 12:43:31'),(322419,'– Sewer management • Monitoring and modelling •Treatment of combined sewer overflows • Interaction sewers and wastewater treatment plants • Wastewater treatment • Small scale wastewater treatment','2025-10-21 12:43:31'),(322420,'– Circular economy • Sludge management • Resource efficiency, recovery, recycling and recovery of nutrients • Water use and reuse • System efficiency • Micropollutants and microplastics','2025-10-21 12:43:31'),(322