ienza, intende seguire le politiche e le proposte di modifica normativa connesse al diritto dell\'immigrazione e dell\'asilo In particolare è interessata all\'attuazione concreta dei regolamenti che hanno modificato il CEAS (Sistema comune di asilo nell\'UE) approvati nel maggio di quest\'anno e al processo di progressiva implementazione fino alla loro piena entrata in vigore nel 2026 Come organizzazione italiana di tutela dei diritti dei rifugiati appartenente a un Paese avente frontiere esterne dell\'Unione, che vede un rilevante ingresso di cittadini provenienti da Paesi terzi che chiedono protezione internazionale, è particolarmente interessata all\'applicazione del Regolamento (UE) n 1348/24 sulle procedure in materia di asilo, del Regolamento (UE) n 1348/24 sulle procedure di rimpatrio alle frontiere, del Regolamento (UE) n 1359/24 sulle situazioni di crisi, del Regolamento (UE) n 1356/24 sugli screening alle frontiere e ovviamente sulla Direttiva rifusa (UE) n 1346/24 in materia di accoglienza In questi settori ICS intende interagire sia con la Commissione Europea che con il Parlamento ed in particolare con la Commissione LIBE e con i gruppi politici che vi sono rappresentati, senza esclusione','2025-10-21 12:50:34'),(324408,'European Parliament report on European Schools','2025-10-21 12:50:35'),(324409,'European Agenda for Tourism 2030','2025-10-21 12:50:36'),(324410,'European Data Strategy','2025-10-21 12:50:36'),(324411,'Transilvania IT Cluster actively engages with various EU legislative proposals and policies aimed at fostering digital innovation, regional development, and technological advancement Our efforts are focused on influencing the formulation and implementation of policies that drive innovation, entrepreneurship and economic growth within the European Union:','2025-10-21 12:50:37'),(324412,'-digital transformation: advocating for policies that promote digitalization across sectors, including initiatives aimed at enhancing digital infrastructure, fostering digital skills development, and accelerating the adoption of emerging technologies','2025-10-21 12:50:37'),(324413,'-regional collaboration: supporting policies that facilitate regional collaboration and cross-border cooperation to strengthen the innovation ecosystem and promote sustainable economic development in transylvania and beyond','2025-10-21 12:50:37'),(324414,'-entrepreneurship and smes: engaging with legislative proposals that support the growth and competitiveness of small and medium-sized enterprises (smes) through innovation-friendly regulations, access to funding, and support programs','2025-10-21 12:50:37'),(324415,'-research and innovation: contributing to initiatives that promote research and innovation excellence, facilitate technology transfer, and enhance the participation of smes and startups in eu-funded research and innovation programs','2025-10-21 12:50:37'),(324416,'-digital single market: advocating for the completion of the digital single market and the removal of barriers to cross-border trade, digital services, and e-commerce, thereby fostering a competitive and inclusive digital economy in europe','2025-10-21 12:50:37'),(324417,'-data protection and privacy: supporting legislative efforts to safeguard data protection rights, enhance privacy standards, and promote trust in digital technologies, in line with eu data protection regulations and standards','2025-10-21 12:50:37'),(324418,'ex Digital Europe Programme, Horizon Europe Framework Programme, European Green Deal, Digital Services Act (DSA), Digital Markets Act (DMA), European Data Strategy, European Artificial Intelligence Act (AIA), European Cloud Initiative, NextGenerationEU Recovery Plan, SME Strategy for a Sustainable and Digital Europe, European Skills Agenda for Sustainable Competitiveness, The European Pillar of Social Rights Action Plan, European Strategy for Data, Single Market Strategy and any others related to the following areas of focus','2025-10-21 12:50:3