 (Digital Services Act, AI Act)','2025-10-21 12:50:42'),(324431,'• Digital Education Action Plan','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324432,'• Erasmus without paper','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324433,'• Erasmus+ programme','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324434,'• European degree','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324435,'• European Education Area','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324436,'• European Excellence initiative','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324437,'• European Green Deal','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324438,'• European Higher Education Area','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324439,'• European Institute of Innovation & Technology','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324440,'• European Research Area','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324441,'• European Skills Agenda','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324442,'• European Strategy for Universities','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324443,'• European Student Card Initiative','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324444,'• Horizon Europe / R&I Framework programme','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324445,'• Legal statute for alliances of higher education institutions','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324446,'• Micro-credentials','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324447,'• Open Science','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324448,'• Qualification and credits recognition','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324449,'• Quality Assurance','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324450,'• Union of Skills','2025-10-21 12:50:43'),(324451,'Fertilising Products Regulation','2025-10-21 12:50:44'),(324452,'Sustainable Food Systems','2025-10-21 12:50:44'),(324453,'Strategic Dialogue on the Future of Agriculture','2025-10-21 12:50:44'),(324454,'Vision for Agriculture and Food','2025-10-21 12:50:44'),(324455,'EarthCheck is a global leader in science-based sustainability certification, ESG advisory, and climate planning for the tourism sector Operating in over 70 countries, EarthCheck helps destinations, businesses, and governments transition to low-carbon, resource-efficient, and socially responsible models Our work aligns with the objectives of key EU legislative frameworks that aim to enhance environmental transparency, improve ESG reporting, and support circular economy principles','2025-10-21 12:50:45'),(324456,'We actively support the intent of the EU Green Claims Directive, offering validated sustainability certification that helps eliminate misleading claims Our work also aligns with the Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive (CSRD), by providing structured ESG benchmarking and reporting tools for both companies and government agencies','2025-10-21 12:50:45'),(324457,'EarthCheck contributes to the goals of the EU Taxonomy Regulation and the Sustainable Finance Disclosure Regulation (SFDR) through ESG data and performance metrics that enable sustainable investment decisions across tourism and hospitality portfolios We also support implementation of the Sustainable Products Initiative and the Ecodesign for Sustainable Products Regulation (ESPR) via operational benchmarking and lifecycle assessment tools','2025-10-21 12:50:45'),(324458,'In response to the European Climate Law and Energy Efficiency Directive, EarthCheck supports the development of decarbonisation strategies for destinations, infrastructure, and business supply chains We provide Net Zero Roadmaps and climate risk scenario planning, including Scope 1, 2 and 3 emissions tracking Our work also contributes to the EU Strategy for Sustainable and Smart Mobility, through emissions reduction planning and sustainable transport integration at the destination level','2025-10-21 12:50:45'),(324459,'EarthCheck supports the EU Nature Restoration Law through biodiversity assessments, regenerative tourism strategies and land-use planning Our alignment with the Waste Framework Directive includes waste benchmarking and circular economy training, and we track developments under the EU Digital Product Passport, advocating for interoperable, secure sustainability data systems in tourism','2025-10-21 12:50:45'),(324460,'We also follow the Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive (CSDDD), supporting businesses and destinations to manage environmental and human rights risks in tourism supply chains through community engagement frameworks and CSR planning','2025-10-21 12:50:45'),(324461,'In addition to regulatory alignment, EarthCheck provides technical support, strategic advisory, and capacity building across ESG, biodiversity, and climate resilience We work with national and local governments to develop Destination Sustainability Action Plans and Decarbonisation Pathways, and we deliver accredited training and professional development programs to build local capability Our EventCheck program supports sustainable event delivery, and we collaborate with academic partners to advance research in climate science, tourism decarbonisation, and sustainable development','2025-10-21 12:50:45'),(324462,'EarthCheck’s work directly supports the ambitions of the EU Green Deal, the Circular Economy Action Plan, and the broader Fit for 55 package Our goal is to enable a sustainable, transparent, and low-impact future for the tourism sector in Europe and globally','2025-10-21 12:50:45'),(324463,'- Objectifs et politiques de décarbonation de l\'UE','2025-10-21 12:50:46'),(324464,'- FuelEU Maritime','2025-10-21 12:50:46'),(324465,'- MRV','2025-10-21 12:50:46'),(324466,'- Aides d\'Etat','2025-10-21 12:50:46'),(324467,'- Industrial Maritime Strategy','2025-10-21 12:50:46'),(324468,'- Sanctions internationales','2025-10-21 12:50:46'),(324469,'- Démarches douanières','2025-10-21 12:50:46'),(324470,'- Politiques multimodales','2025-10-21 12:50:46'),(324471,'- Conditions de travail et aspects sociaux, formation','2025-10-21 12:50:46'),(324472,'- Pavillons maritimes','2025-10-21 12:50:46'),(324473,'Our consultancy focuses on EU legislative proposals and policies related to digital regulation, AI governance, consumer protection, and platform accountability Key areas of engagement include the AI Act, particularly Article 5 on prohibited practices, the Digital Services Act (DSA) and Digital Markets Act (DMA), as well as regulatory frameworks addressing dark patterns, algorithmic transparency, and deceptive design We contribute to discussions on child protection in digital environments, online disinformation, and the regulation of manipulative system architectures Our work also intersects with data protection laws, such as the GDPR, and emerging EU initiatives on AI liability, fairness, and fundamental rights in the digital sphere','2025-10-21 12:50:47'),(324474,'Vehicle electrification trends, including regulations that support electrified power trains, e-cooling and hydrogen fuel cell mobility Light- and heavy-duty vehicle emissions regulations, including CO2 and criteria pollutants Chemicals regulation, when impacting our products and any aspect regarding Competitiveness, Trade and Sustainability','2025-10-21 12:50:48'),(324475,'Activity is channeled mainly through BirdLife Europe, Bryssels','2025-10-21 12:50:49'),(324476,'Complains to commission about  breach of the Union law','2025-10-21 12:50:49'),(324477,'Natureprotection legislation, Common agriculture policy, Bioenergy legislation, Green deal, Ban of lead in hunting','2025-10-21 12:50:49'),(324478,'Implementation of the Biocidal Products Regulation','2025-10-21 12:50:51'),(324479,'Mandatory Country of Origin Labelling for ingredients','2025-10-21 12:50:51'),(324480,'REFIT General Food Law','2025-10-21 12:50:51'),(324481,'EIP on Raw Materials','2025-10-21 12:50:51'),(324482,'Energy related issues','2025-10-21 12:50:51'),(324483,'Rules on organic production of salt','2025-10-21 12:50:51'),(324484,'Promocja rynku usług energetycznych, poprawy efektywności energetycznej w budynkach, w przedsiębiorstwach, zrównoważony rozwój, wsparcie samorządności oraz polityk miejskich Realizacja zasady partnerstwa w wydatkowaniu funduszy publicznych tak UE  jak i krajowych','2025-10-21 12:50:52'),(324485,'DIGITAL AND SINGLE MARKET STRATEGY – Our members are multi-channel retailers We seek to ensure that EU policy respects a level playing field for all retail channels and that all independent retailers as well as groups thereof can efficiently operate on- and offline, and are able to compete on fair terms Due to their business model, the websites of groups of independent retailers are by nature platforms These closed platforms of EU-based member retailers present no more risk to consumers than their brick and mortar stores Issues: Fair digital market, payment systems, digital euro, Digital Product Passport, cybersecurity, AI, Single Market Act, DSA, Data Act, product liability, consumer protection online, simplification…','2025-10-21 12:50:53'),(324486,'SUSTAINABILITY – Sustainability legislation needs to be practicable, effective and efficient Sustainability has a cost, which particularly affects SME retailers We seek to any unnecessary or disproportionate burdens and costs for independent retailers and simplification of EU legislation Where possible, burdens should be borne at group level in line with the logic of the cooperative business model of the groups Issues: Omnibus proposals, due diligence, non-financial reporting, circular economy, Farm to Fork Strategy, energy efficiency, eco and energy labelling, green claims, waste (food waste, PPWR, EPR, textile waste), eco-design, Digital Product Passport, deforestation…','2025-10-21 12:50:53'),(324487,'INDUSTRIAL STRATEGY/RETAIL ECOSYSTEM – Independent retail constitutes a very large part of the retail market We seek to ensure that the strategy benefits and reflects the needs of independent retailers, their groups, and consumers Issues: Transition pathways for retail and agri-food, diverse retail market, healthy cities and rural areas, SME strategy, SME financing, entrepreneurship, skills and jobs, B2B trading practices, supply chain transparency, simplification of legislation','2025-10-21 12:50:53'),(324488,'CONSUMER PROTECTION – Our members are committed to ensuring consumer safety and health This is essential for their close relationships with customers and their reputation We seek clear, understandable rules that can be easily implemented and do not constitute unnecessary burdens on SME retailers Issues: Product safety and liability, labelling (ecolabelling, energy labelling, NutriScore, green claims), healthy food, packaging, consumer contracts, Digital Product Passport, right to repair…','2025-10-21 12:50:53'),(324489,'COMPETITION RULES – The central (wholesale) organisations of groups of independent retailers as well as each member retailer are separate legal entities, whereby the central organisations act at a different economic level of the chain than their SME member retailers, vertical agreements between these organisations and their retailers are indispensable to their functioning These agreements concern eg information exchange, joint purchasing and commercialisation and standardisation Their pro-competitive effects benefit consumers On a horizontal level, the retailers are independent entrepreneurs and competitors in the same catchment area Due to this, agreements in groups of independent retailers are subject to the Vertical Block Exemption Regulation and Guidelines, and the Guidelines on Horizontal Agreements This has a disproportionate negative impact on their competitiveness, particularly in a digital market, in comparison to their main competitors, integrated retail chains, whose internal activities are not limited by these rules We seek a fairer treatment of group structures under competition rules to heighten competition and consumer benefit Issues: VBER, the VGL and HGL, single-price platforms, selective distribution, dual distribution, dual pricing, joint purchasing, alliances, territorial supply constraints, market definition, DMA, merger rules…','2025-10-21 12:50:53'),(324490,'- REACH implementation','2025-10-21 12:50:56'),(324491,'- Classification, Labelling and Packaging of substances and mixtures (CLP)','2025-10-21 12:50:56'),(324492,'- Biocidal products','2025-10-2