l issues and most importantly, Youth inclusion and participation in a direct dialogue with policy- and decision-makers','2025-10-21 12:53:43'),(325286,'We strongly believe in a sustainable future and we think the EU needs to have a major role in building it This is why the main policies followed by our organisation are the ones connected to free movement, democracy, youth mobility, environmental and social justice The role of Europe in the world is very relevant as well to ensure human rights and to promote peace We believe that the way to achieve the goals above mentioned, is through the formation of a European democratic Federation','2025-10-21 12:53:43'),(325287,'Our political proposals are drafted through a bottom up approach by three political committees, focused on institutions and governance, internal european affairs, and external affairs and global governance The resolutions defined by these participatory bodies are then used by the Executive Board to build up legislative proposals and advocacy actions towards the EU Institutions','2025-10-21 12:53:43'),(325288,'Policy Papers are available at https://healthyeuropeeu/policy/ and manifesto available at https://healthyeuropeeu/european-well-being-deal/','2025-10-21 12:53:44'),(325289,'Focus on Digital Health, Environmental Health, Human Health and the Economy of Well-being','2025-10-21 12:53:44'),(325290,'- Audiovisuaaliset mediapalvelut','2025-10-21 12:53:45'),(325291,'- Digitaaliset sisämarkkinat (DSM ja DSA)','2025-10-21 12:53:45'),(325292,'- Rahanpesun vastainen toiminta','2025-10-21 12:53:45'),(325293,'- Jäsenvaltioiden arpajaislainsäädännöt','2025-10-21 12:53:45'),(325294,'- Digitaalinen verotus','2025-10-21 12:53:45'),(325295,'- Rahapelien toimeenpano','2025-10-21 12:53:45'),(325296,'Revision of the General Pharmaceutical Legislation, implementation of the EU Regulation on HTA, Clinical Trials legislation, Europe\'s Beating Cancer Plan,  implementation of the EHDS Regulation, IP Action Plan, cross-count