ity Due Dilligence Directive - Omnibus I - COM(2025)81 Proposal postponing the application of some reporting requirements in the Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive and the transposition deadline and application of the Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive - Omnibus I - COM(2025)80 Gas Storage Regulation – 2025/0051 (COD)','2025-10-21 12:55:44'),(325782,'Directive 2023/959 amending the EU Emissions Trading System Regulation 2023/956 establishing a carbon border adjustment mechanism Communication on Europe\'s 2040 climate target and path to climate neutrality by 2050 - COM(2024) 63 Industrial Carbon Management Strategy - COM/2024/62 Regulation 2024/3012 establishing a Union certification framework for permanent carbon removals, carbon farming and carbon storage in products Proposal for a Green Claims Directive - 2023/0085 (COD) Regulation on methane emissions reduction in the energy sector - COM(2021) 805 Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/1184 establishing a Union methodology setting out detailed rules for the production of RFNBOs Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/1185 establishing a minimum threshold for GHG emissions savings of recycled carbon fuels and by specifying a methodology for assessing GHG emissions savings from RFNBOs and recycled carbon fuels Regulation (EU) 2022/2578 establishing a market correction mechanism to protect Union citizens and the economy against excessively high prices Directive 2023/2413 on the promotion of energy from renewable sources Regulation 2023/1804on the deployment of alternative fuels infrastructure Delegated Directive 2024/1405 amending Annex IX to Directive 2018/2001 as regards adding feedstock for the production of biofuels and biogas Regulation 2023/839 on CO₂ emission performance standards for cars and vans Regulation CO₂ emission performance standards for heavy-duty vehicles COM(2023)88 Regulation 2024/1747 to improve the Union’s electricity market design Commission Recommendation on auction design for renewable energy - C/2024/2650 Regulation 2024/1735 establishing a framework of measures for strengthening Europe’s net-zero technology manufacturing ecosystem Regulation 2023/2405 on sustainable air transport Regulation 2023/1805 on the use of renewable and low-carbon fuels in maritime transport Regulation 2025/40 on packaging and packaging waste Regulation 1907/2006 concerning the Registration, Evaluation, Authorisation and Restriction of Chemicals (REACH)','2025-10-21 12:55:44'),(325783,'We are interested in initiatives relating to the promotion of investment in the real economy, the financing of infrastructure (specifically commercial real estate, including commercially owned and operated rental housing) and the built environment, and long-term investment','2025-10-21 12:55:56'),(325784,'We are particularly interested in elements of the Capital Markets Union, such as the revival of the securitisation market for exposures such as commercial mortgage-backed securities (CMBS) which have unfortunately been classified as irredeemably \"non-STS\" and therefore give rise to penal capital charges under the Solvency II SCR','2025-10-21 12:55:56'),(325785,'Other financial sector regulation affecting commercial real estate lending, such as regulation of banks (eg via CRR implementing Basel III finalisation), insurers (the Solvency II SCR point mentioned above), and alternative investment fund managers investing in commercial real estate debt or advancing commercial real estate loans We are interested in proposals relating to the regulation and oversight of non-bank financial intermediaries (NBFIs), an important source of credit for real estate markets to the extent that banks reduce their participation','2025-10-21 12:55:56'),(325786,'We are interested in real estate and financial market data and transparency, including through efforts (such as by the ESRB) to define, understand, monitor and manage financial system risks arising from the commercial real estate (debt) market','2025-10-21 12:55:56'),(325787,'We are increasingly focused on how commercial real estate finance markets can reflect and promote environmental, social and governance (ESG) considerations, including through \'green\' lending to encourage the decarbonisation of the built environment, as well as improving the diversity and inclusiveness of our industry Related data sharing and disclosures, SFDR, EU Taxonomy and similar initiatives are therefore of interest We participated in the EEFIG working group on Energy Efficiency First in this context','2025-10-21 12:55:56'),(325788,'A growing representation of passive debt investors and real estate investment firms in our membership is broadening and driving our agenda to ensure that the commercial real estate lending industry remains connected to the concerns of those two critical external stakeholder groups (In other words, not only do we not represent any particular constituency of lenders at the expense of others we do not represent lenders at the expense of their borrowers or those allocating capital to the lenders We are focused on the market as a whole)','2025-10-21 12:55:56'),(325789,'Transport and mobility files such as:','2025-10-21 12:55:57'),(325790,'European Green Deal: Implementation \'\'Fit for 55\'\' Package, Air quality Euro 7, End of Life Vehicles','2025-10-21 12:55:57'),(325791,'Digitisation: Access to in-vehicle data, European Mobility Data Space, Artificial Intelligence, Connected and Automated Mobility','2025-10-21 12:55:57'),(325792,'Urban mobility: Micro-mobility, Urban Mobility Framework, new mobility trends','2025-10-21 12:55:57'),(325793,'Road safety: Road Safety Package, General Safety Regulation','2025-10-21 12:55:57'),(325794,'Social aspects of the twin transitions','2025-10-21 12:55:57'),(325795,'Global Europe: Neighbourhood, Development and International Cooperation Instrument - NDICI - Partenariats Internationaux','2025-10-21 12:55:58'),(325796,'Accords de partenariat économique avec les pays ACP','2025-10-21 12:55:58'),(325797,'Relations UE - ACP','2025-10-21 12:55:58'),(325798,'European Pillar of Social Rights','2025-10-21 12:55:59'),(325799,'Social Inclusion','2025-10-21 12:55:59'),(325800,'Social Economy Action Plan','2025-10-21 12:55:59'),(325801,'WEEE Directive','2025-10-21 12:55:59'),(325802,'Extended Producer Responsibility','2025-10-21 12:55:59'),(325803,'Ecodesign','2025-10-21 12:55:59'),(325804,'Public Procurement','2025-10-21 12:55:59'),(325805,'State aid','2025-10-21 12:55:59'),(325806,'Regional policies','2025-10-21 12:55:59'),(325807,'- DSM','2025-10-21 12:56:01'),(325808,'- eIDAS','2025-10-21 12:56:01'),(325809,'Urban Waste Water Treatment Directive (Recast, Directive (EU) 2024/3019)','2025-10-21 12:56:02'),(325810,'Water Framework Directive and Groundwater Directive Updates','2025-10-21 12:56:02'),(325811,'Nature Restoration Law (Regulation (EU) 2024/1991)','2025-10-21 12:56:02'),(325812,'Drinking Water Directive (Directive (EU) 2020/2184)','2025-10-21 12:56:02'),(325813,'REGULATION (EU) 2020/741 OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL of 25 May 2020  on minimum requirements for water reuse','2025-10-21 12:56:02'),(325814,'N/A we have not focused on any specific policies yet But we have a clear policy ask and invite for governments around the world where we list the following:','2025-10-21 12:56:03'),(325815,'1 Establishing equal, fully paid, non-transferable parental leave for all parents, in addition to maternity leave and care days','2025-10-21 12:56:03'),(325816,'2 Providing state-supported, high-quality childcare that facilitates the full participation in economic activities for all working parents and caregivers','2025-10-21 12:56:03'),(325817,'3 Transforming health sector institutions to promote fathers’ involvement from the prenatal period through birth and childhood and men’s involvement as caregivers','2025-10-21 12:56:03'),(325818,'4 Establishing national care policies and campaigns that recognize, reduce, and redistribute care work equally between men and women','2025-10-21 12:56:03'),(325819,'5 Expanding social protection programs to redistribute care equally between women and men who are unemployed or working in the informal economy, while keeping a focus on the needs and rights of women and girls','2025-10-21 12:56:03'),(325820,'IDEA Innovation Center is particularly interested in EU initiatives that facilitate startup access to equity and risk finance Of particular relevance are the European Long-Term Investment Funds (ELTIFs), the InvestEU Programme—especially its SME window—and the EU Listing Acts, which aim to simplify SME listings These instruments are seen as valuable enablers for early-stage ventures seeking sustainable growth and market entry','2025-10-21 12:56:03'),(325821,'Also, we see relevance in the Crowdfunding Regulation to improve cross-boarder access to private investment','2025-10-21 12:56:03'),(325822,'Digital market Act','2025-10-21 12:56:05'),(325823,'Digital Data Act','2025-10-21 12:56:05'),(325824,'Prawo Autorskie','2025-10-21 12:56:05'),(325825,'MoU on online advertising and IP infringement','2025-10-21 12:56:05'),(325826,'Digital Content Directive & New Deal for Consumers','2025-10-21 12:56:05'),(325827,'Online Disinformation Code of Practice','2025-10-21 12:56:05'),(325828,'Platforms to Business Regulation','2025-10-21 12:56:05'),(325829,'Political Advertising','2025-10-21 12:56:05'),(325830,'Media Freedom Act','2025-10-21 12:56:05'),(325831,'- EU animal welfare policy issues','2025-10-21 12:56:06'),(325832,'- Animal agriculture and sustainable food policy','2025-10-21 12:56:06'),(325833,'- Wildlife trade policy and CITES','2025-10-21 12:56:06'),(325834,'- Biodiversity policy, especially coexistence with large carnivores','2025-10-21 12:56:06'),(325835,'- Policy relating to protection of marine mammals','2025-10-21 12:56:06'),(325836,'- EU policy relating to use of animals in scientific research and animal alternatives, including chemic