 robust financial sector and banking regulation framework as well as to foster harmonized, consistent and convergent regulatory and supervisory culture and practices In that regard, financial stability, sustainable economic growth and job creation forms an integral part of CaixaBank’s corporate responsibility when dealing with European affairs','2025-10-21 12:57:14'),(326068,'In particular, areas of direct interest include, among others, banking and prudential regulation (Banking Union initiatives, CRR/CRD, BRRD), accounting framework (IFRS), market related initiatives (CMU inititatives, MIFID, IDD), retail payments legislation (PSD), Innovation initiatives (FinTech Action Plan), Sustainable Finance Action Plan, AML framework,…','2025-10-21 12:57:14'),(326069,'Prudential: Solvency II Insurance Recovery and Resolution Directive (IRRD) Sustainable Finance: Taxonomy Sustainable Finance Disclosure Regulation (SFDR) Corporate Sustainable Due Diligence Directive (CSDDD) Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive (CSRD) Consumer Protection: Anti-discrimination Insurance Distribution Directive (IDD) Package Retail and Insurance-based Investment Products (PRIIPs) Markets in Financial Instruments Directive (MiFID) Retail Investment Strategy (RIS) Digital: Data Protection Artificial Intelligence (AI Act) European Health Data Space (EHDS) Financial Data Access (FiDA) Capital Markets Union (CMU): Pensions Supervision Securitization Pan-European Pension Plan (PEPP) Financial Crime: Anti-Money Laundering (AML) Sanctions Taxation: VAT in the Digital Age (ViDA) DAC 9 Business in Europe: Framework for Income Taxation (BEFIT) Trade credit insurance: Late Payment Asset management: European Market Infrastructure Regulation (EMIR) Markets in Financial Instruments Regulation (MiFIR) Alternative Investment Funds Managers Directive (AIFMD) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities Directive (UCITS) European Long Term Investment Fund (ELTIF)','2025-10-21 12:57:17'),