ing technical depth with legal and ethical oversight','2025-10-21 13:02:03'),(327067,'Behind the scenes, the platform operates through three synchronized processes:','2025-10-21 13:02:03'),(327068,'1 Analytical layer — methodology and taxonomy, curated over 9 years, generating 500M+ unique insights to map and score AI systems across policy, business, ethical, and legal dimensions','2025-10-21 13:02:03'),(327069,'2 Test agents —  technical modules that validate fairness, privacy, security, robustness, and performance for LLMs and predictive models All according to the EU AI Act','2025-10-21 13:02:03'),(327070,'3 Policy controls according to the AI Act — Built-in governance rules that enforce development protocols, flag exceptions, and trace decisions back to organizational accountability','2025-10-21 13:02:03'),(327071,'“The Asenion fast-track for AI Act Governance will strengthen EU competitive power and at the same time provide pricing that is not only for the few”','2025-10-21 13:02:03'),(327072,'Anna Felländer, co-founder and President Asenion Europe','2025-10-21 13:02:03'),(327073,'- Creative Europe programme 2021–2027','2025-10-21 13:02:04'),(327074,'- Directive sur le droit d\'auteur dans le marché unique numérique','2025-10-21 13:02:04'),(327075,'-Artificial Intelligence Act','2025-10-21 13:02:04'),(327076,'-Audiovisual Media Service Directive (AVMSD)','2025-10-21 13:02:04'),(327077,'-Directive sur la diffusion en ligne et les retransmissions','2025-10-21 13:02:04'),(327078,'- EU-ETS: industrial, heat, transport, and shipping sectors EU-ETS reform','2025-10-21 13:02:05'),(327079,'- RePower EU','2025-10-21 13:02:05'),(327080,'- FuelEU maritime regulation','2025-10-21 13:02:05'),(327081,'- ReFuelEU Aviation regulation','2025-10-21 13:02:05'),(327082,'- Carbon Removals and Carbon Farming Directive','2025-10-21 13:02:05'),(327083,'EU CRCF - carbon removal framework, Green Claims, other EC climate actions','2025-10-21 13:02:06'),(327084,'Päämääriensä tavoittamiseksi yhdistys:','2025-10-21 13:02:07'),(327085,'- pitää yhteyttä EU:n ja Suomen julkiseen hallintoon ja politiikkoihin, energia-alan yrityksiin, järjestöihin, tiedotusvälineisiin sekä tutkimus- ja oppilaitoksiin,','2025-10-21 13:02:07'),(327086,'- tekee energia-alaan liittyviä aloitteita ja esityksiä EU:n ja Suomen julkiselle hallinnolle sekä antaa energiankäyttäjien asemaa koskevia lausuntoja ja kannanottoja,','2025-10-21 13:02:07'),(327087,'- tekee yhteistyötä  Euroopan Unionin, Pohjoismaiden ja Suomen tasolla toimivien osapuolten kanssa ja tarvittaessa edustaa niissä jäseniään','2025-10-21 13:02:07'),(327088,'EU Action Plan on Human Rights and Democracy','2025-10-21 13:02:08'),(327089,'A new agenda for the Mediterranean','2025-10-21 13:02:08'),(327090,'on plants obtained by certain new genomic techniques and their food and feed, and','2025-10-21 13:02:08'),(327091,'amending Regulation (EU) 2017/625','2025-10-21 13:02:08'),(327092,'COMMUNICATION FROM THE COMMISSION TO THE EUROPEAN','2025-10-21 13:02:08'),(327093,'PARLIAMENT, THE COUNCIL, THE EUROPEAN ECONOMIC AND SOCIAL','2025-10-21 13:02:08'),(327094,'COMMITTEE AND THE COMMITTEE OF THE REGIONS','2025-10-21 13:02:08'),(327095,'A Vision for Agriculture and Food','2025-10-21 13:02:08'),(327096,'Shaping together an attractive farming and agri-food sector for future generations','2025-10-21 13:02:08'),(327097,'Die Tourismus-Servicestelle beantwortet täglich individuelle Anfragen von Stakeholdern hinsichtlich der Anwendung der neuen Regelungen, direkte Anfragen der Branche und auch Beantwortung von Anfragen von Reisenden Weiters zeigt sie Problemfelder zu nationalen, europäischen und internationalen Vorhaben auf und verabschiedet ausführliche Stellungnahmen aus touristischer Sicht','2025-10-21 13:02:09'),(327098,'ATR closely monitors EU initiatives, policies and legislative initiatives that can impact its activity Most of them are related to aviation industry (safety, certification, EASA functioning…), international agreements (Trade Agreements, Bilateral Safety Agreements, Aviation Comprehensive Agreements…), environment, and R&D programs','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327099,'For instance, ATR has a particular interest in understanding and following the following procedures (this is a non-exhaustive list that can be subject to modification following EU initiatives, policies and legislative files release and/or update):','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327100,'-       Sustainable aviation fuels – ReFuelEU Aviation','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327101,'-       Environmental Label Programme - EASA','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327102,'-	REACH ((EC) No 1907/2006 – 18122006)','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327103,'-	Legislation about Public Service Obligations (PSO) - 1008/2008','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327104,'-	EU Circular Economy Package','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327105,'-	Emissions Trading System – ETS','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327106,'-	Horizon2020','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327107,'-	Clean Sky','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327108,'-	SESAR','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327109,'-       Green Industrial Plan','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327110,'-       Non-CO2 MRV','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327111,'-       NZIA','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327112,'-       Taxonomy','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327113,'-       CSRD','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327114,'-       CS3D','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327115,'-       CBAM','2025-10-21 13:02:10'),(327116,'Grid reform, alternative fuels and infrastructure, electric vehicles, infrastructure, trade, renewable energy, energy storage, VAT, taxation, cross-border relations, transportation, payments (business and consumer)','2025-10-21 13:02:11'),(327117,'Medical Device Regulation 2017/745','2025-10-21 13:02:12'),(327118,'European Union directive 2014/85/EU on driver licensing in obstructive sleep apnoea:','2025-10-21 13:02:12'),(327119,'Call for expressions of interest from EU/EEA/Western Balkans-based businesses to invest in the Western Balkans - https://enlargementeceuropaeu/enlargement-policy/enhanced-eu-engagement-western-balkans/publication-call-expressions-interest-eueeawestern-balkans-based-businesses-invest-western-balkans_en','2025-10-21 13:02:13'),(327120,'DIRETTIVA 2014/95/UE DEL PARLAMENTO EUROPEO E DEL CONSIGLIO del 22 ottobre 2014 recante modifica della direttiva 2013/34/UE per quanto riguarda la comunicazione di informazioni di carattere non finanziario e di informazioni sulla diversità da parte di talune imprese e di taluni gruppi di grandi dimensioni','2025-10-21 13:02:14'),(327121,'Direttiva 2000/78/CE del Consiglio, del 27 novembre 2000, che stabilisce un quadro generale per la parità di trattamento in materia di occupazione e di condizioni di lavoro','2025-10-21 13:02:14'),(327122,'Direttiva 2000/43/CE del Consiglio, del 29 giugno 2000, che attua il principio della parità di trattamento fra le persone indipendentemente dalla razza e dall\'origine etnica','2025-10-21 13:02:14'),(327123,'Convenzione del Consiglio d\'Europa sulla prevenzione e la lotta contro la violenza nei confronti delle donne e la violenza domestica (Convenzione di Istanbul)','2025-10-21 13:02:14'),(327124,'Risoluzione del Parlamento europeo del 14 febbraio 2019 sul futuro dell\'elenco di azioni a favore delle persone LGBTI (2019‑2024)','2025-10-21 13:02:14'),(327125,'EU Action Plan on Human Rights and Democracy 2015- 2019, adopted by the Council of the European Union in July 2015”','2025-10-21 13:02:14'),(327126,'Committee of Ministers of Council of Europe CM/Rec(2016)3 to the Member States on human Rights and business','2025-10-21 13:02:14'),(327127,'Influenza diretta delle politiche Comunitare in materia di gestione ambientale attraverso l\' interazione con le Istituzioni del Comando Unità Forestali Ambientali e Agroalimentari (CUFAA) dell\'Arma dei Carabinieri e attraverso sensibilizzazione diretta di Parlamentari Nazionali ed Europei sulle pertinenti politiche legislative Europee','2025-10-21 13:02:15'),(327128,'Direttive seguite Direttiva 2009/147 CE sulla protezione dell\' avifauna omeoterma Habitats Directive, Birds Directive, Water Framework Directive, Marine Strategy Framework Directive, Floods Directive','2025-10-21 13:02:15'),(327129,'Influenza indiretta delle politiche Comunitarie in materia ambientale, attraverso pubblici simposi, eventi, seminari e conferenze a livello nazionale, europeo ed internazionale per la sensibilizzazione dell\' opinione pubblica sulle tematiche della protezione ambientale','2025-10-21 13:02:15'),(327130,'Erasmus +, KA102, že 15 let','2025-10-21 13:02:16'),(327131,'We influence indirectly policy implementation and decision-making in the and the European Commission through being member of IT Working group in E+','2025-10-21 13:02:16'),(327132,'Our main interests are in all policies related to landscape development, cultural heritage environment and public sports / public health','2025-10-21 13:02:17'),(327133,'This comprises the CAP (and now also the European Green Deal), especially the attempts to greening the agricultural policy with a specific interest in improving the landscape quality and ensuring the accessibility of the landscape Therefore we are specially interested in the funding schemes governed by EAFRD and ESIF, and how they provide for a better landscape and ensure the accessibility of the landscape In the structural funds and regional development our main interest leis in the LEADER programm, especially in how it can help to improve the quality of the landscape and Eco-Tourism We are also interested in avoiding conflicts between developments and the interest of charities and volunteer organizations in the field, which are again and again creeping up in LEADER funding schemes We are especially interested in the Environment Impact Assessment as many of our national members are registered environmental organizations active in the consultation processes of planning and development projects in the framework of the EIA regulations Here we are advocating again for the interests of the landscape and the accessibility of the landscape','2025-10-21 13:02:17'),(327134,'In the field of cultural heritage and sport we mainly interested in the ERASMUS+ regulations and how these funding schemes help to preserve and enhance the quality of landscape as well as every day sport activities, especially of course hiking and related activities We are also interested in the European Agenda for Culture We are actually participating in ERASMUS+ projects setting standards for Good Governance in Sport, where we advocate especially for the protection of minors and young people as well as inclusiveness with the main focus on sport for everyone and sport carried out in volunteer associations','2025-10-21 13:02:17'),(327135,'As a hiking organization we also have a special interest in infrastructure, mainly concerning the foot-paths and foot-traffic / slow traffic We are actually participating in and ERASMUS+ project preparing standards for environment friendly out door activities in the mountain areas of Europe We are open for creating and supporting the projects as European Green Belt We are also advocating for eco tourism and soft tourism and the right to access the landscape for hiking and related out-door activities','2025-10-21 13:02:17'),(327136,'In the field of economy and competition we are interested in specific regulations to protect charities and volunteer organizations, especially in the tax sector and the rules for applying VAT','2025-10-21 13:02:17'),(327137,'We have been active in these fields, but a lot of the work is done through our member organisations, as we are an umbrella organisation and rely on the support of our members','2025-10-21 13:02:17'),(327138,'Actual consultations we are especially interested in are eg Evaluation of the Common Agricultural Policy’s impact on territorial development of rural areas: socioeconomic aspects or the Evaluation of the impacts of the CAP on habitats, landscape, biodiversity','2025-10-21 13:02:17'),(327139,'One of the key objectives of the \'Business for Business\' is to help companies maximize the benefits of the DCFTA Another objective is to advocate for business\' interests on various local and international platforms, while also addressing the necessary progress in economic reforms, as outlined in the EU Commission\'s 2023 Report on Georgia, to bring Georgian legislation closer to the EU acquis','2025-10-21 13:02:18'),(327140,'One of the key focus areas for \'Business for Business\' is promoting Sustainable Connectivity, aligned with EU transport policy (Chapter 14) This involves actively supporting Georgia in aligning with and implementing the transport acquis across all sectors and levels of government Another priority is fostering Competition, in line with EU Competition Policy (Chapter 8), by contributing to the harmonization of Georgia’s legal framework on antitrust, mergers, and State aid with the EU acquis Additionally, \'Business for Business\' facilitates SME Internationalization by improving Georgian companies’ access to information about existing EU co-funded instruments and projects in the field of internationalization \'Business for Business\' plans to periodically draft position papers on these key issues and present them to the relevant stakeholders on local and EU Institutions level','2025-10-21 13:02:18'),(327141,'The Libyan Technology Foundation (LTF) follows and contributes to EU digital policies and legislative proposals that promote inclusive, rights-based, and human-centric digital transformation In particular, LTF is interested in initiatives related to the Digital Services Act (DSA), Digital Markets Act (DMA), AI Act, Data Governance Act, Cybersecurity Act, and the EU’s external digital cooperation frameworks, such as the EU–Africa Digital Economy Task Force, the Global Gateway strategy, and the D4D Hub LTF seeks to align its advocacy and project work with EU values on data protection, digital rights, online safety, open technologies, and ethical AI, especially in the context of global digital governance and Euro-Mediterranean cooperation','2025-10-21 13:02:18'),(327142,'France terre d’asile concentre ses activités de représentation d’intérêts sur le Pacte sur la migration et l’asile, présenté par la Commission européenne en septembre 2020, ainsi que sur l’ensemble des propositions législatives qui en découlent','2025-10-21 13:02:19'),(327143,'Ces travaux incluent l’ensemble des textes du Pacte sur la migration et l’asile, couvrant la réforme du régime d’asile européen commun, la gestion de l’asile et de la migration, le mécanisme de solidarité entre États membres, le filtrage aux frontières extérieures, la révision du règlement Eurodac, ainsi que les règles relatives aux conditions d’accueil, aux procédures et à la reconnaissance de la protection internationale','2025-10-21 13:02:19'),(327144,'France terre d’asile suit également de près la mise en œuvre du Pacte sur la migration et l’asile dans ses différentes dimensions législatives, opérationnelles et financières, afin de promouvoir le respect des droits fondamentaux et l’accès effectif à la protection internationales','2025-10-21 13:02:19'),(327145,'France terre d’asile suit également les politiques législatives et initiatives de l’Union européenne relatives à la gestion des migrations avec les pays tiers, notamment les accords de coopération, de réadmission et de partenariat','2025-10-21 13:02:19'),(327146,'- The National Youth Council of Latvia actively follows and contributes to key policy developments at the European level Our advocacy is primarily guided by the EU Youth Strategy 2019-2027 and the subsequent strategies and files related to it As a member of the EU Youth Stakeholders\' Group, we engage directly in discussions on highly relevant documents These include the new Strategy for Intergenerational Fairness, the Action Plan on the European Social Rights, and the developing EU Civil Society Strategy Furthermore, we place high importance on files concerning the Erasmus+ Programme and the Multiannual Financial Framework (MFF), advocating for sustainable funding and opportunities that directly benefit young people Our goal is to proactively shape a European framework that empowers youth and addresses their needs comprehensively','2025-10-21 13:02:20'),(327147,'- Following President von der Leyen’s Political Guidelines 2024-2029, the European Commission has set up the President’s Youth Advisory Board (the ‘Board’) on 25 June The Board will provide advice on ongoing and future Commission policies and initiatives relevant to young people, giving them an opportunity to express their views at the highest level of the Commission The Board will operate in compliance with the horizontal rules on the creation and operation of Commission expert groups This initiative further strengthens the Commission’s efforts to reinforce youth participation at the Union level It builds upon the Commission’s Communication on the European Year of Youth 2022 which reaffirmed the ambition of the Commission to empower young people to actively participate in and shape the Union’s future The Board will be composed of 28 members: the National Youth Council in each EU Member State and the European Youth Forum','2025-10-21 13:02:20'),(327148,'The Scientific and Technological Center for Unmanned Systems (CNTSB) is a Polish SME focused on the development, testing, and implementation of unmanned aerial systems (UAS) and their applications in agriculture, environmental monitoring, public safety, and infrastructure CNTSB operates a certified UAS training center, conducts R&D in AI, robotics, and autonomous systems, and supports the transfer of technology from academia to industry As the coordinator of the Unmanned Systems Cluster, CNTSB builds networks between universities, tech companies, and public institutions The organization offers consulting, integration of drone-based solutions, and participates in EU-funded projects CNTSB is also active in policy advisory and standardization work related to drone legislation at national and EU level Its mission is to promote responsible, safe, and sustainable use of drone technologies across sectors','2025-10-21 13:02:21'),(327149,'Towarowa Giełda Energii SA carefully follows all European Commission activities and legislative files pertainig to the establishment of Energy Union and Internal Energy Market Through membership in industry associations, TGE follows the drafting of various electricity Network Codes and associated Guidelines and the new European Gas Target Model Furthermore, TGE is involved in: the implementation of Regulation 1227/2011 (REMIT) (TGE is member to various roundtables organised by Agency for Cooperation of Energy Regulators) the implementation of Directive 2014/65 (MiFID II) and Regulation 600/2014 (MiFIR) the implementation of Directive 2003/6/EC (MAD) and Regulation (EU) No 596/2014 (MAR) and all other consultation papers pertaining to regulation of commodity derivatives and financial instruments','2025-10-21 13:02:22'),(327150,'The Critical Medicines Act aims to mitigate drug shortages in the EU To achieve this, we propose implementing a proven and scalable Healthcare Utility model This model has been shown to effectively address drug shortages and will significantly improve the resilience of critical medicine supply chains within the EU','2025-10-21 13:02:22'),(327151,'The Healthcare Utility Model is more than a concept—it’s a movement to rewrite the rules of healthcare for billions By harnessing the ingenuity and rapid pace of private-sector entrepreneurial innovation, It doesn’t just create another technical solution it creates a sustainable, scalable system that redefines access, equity, and impact in healthcare Be part of this transformation','2025-10-21 13:02:22'),(327152,'Review of the Mortgage Credit Directive','2025-10-21 13:02:23'),(327153,'Interpretation of the Capital Requirements Regulation','2025-10-21 13:02:23'),(327154,'Valuation aspects of EU 