e all’interno di reti scientifiche europee ed internazionali','2025-10-21 13:09:44'),(329219,'Food contact legislation EU regulation 10/2011 and EU regulation 1935/2004 and EU regulation 2024/3190','2025-10-21 13:09:45'),(329220,'Reach regulation 1907/2006','2025-10-21 13:09:45'),(329221,'BPR regulation 528/2012','2025-10-21 13:09:45'),(329222,'Schaffung von politischen und wirtschaftlichen Rahmenbedingungen die einen Wiederaufbau der europäischen Solarindustrie ermöglichen','2025-10-21 13:09:45'),(329223,'COM (2022) 209: Proposal for a REGULATION OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL laying down rules to prevent and combat child sexual abuse','2025-10-21 13:09:46'),(329224,'https://eur-lexeuropaeu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=COM%3A2022%3A209%3AFIN&qid=1652451192472','2025-10-21 13:09:46'),(329225,'COM/2024/60: Proposal for a DIRECTIVE OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL on combating the sexual abuse and sexual exploitation of children and child sexual abuse material and replacing Council Framework Decision 2004/68/JHA (recast)','2025-10-21 13:09:46'),(329226,'https://eur-lexeuropaeu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=COM%3A2024%3A60%3AFIN','2025-10-21 13:09:46'),(329227,'While additional and future regulation may have relevance to us (eg EU Deforestation Regulation and its interaction with Child and Forced Labour), the main target legislation is the Forced Labour Regulation ie','2025-10-21 13:09:50'),(329228,'\"REGULATION (EU) 2024/3015 OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL of 27 November 2024 on prohibiting products made with forced labour on the Union market and amending Directive (EU) 2019/1937\"','2025-10-21 13:09:50'),(329229,'Defending the interests of IPF patients at European level with emphasis on:','2025-10-21 13:09:51'),(329230,'- access to treatment and services, including non-pharmacological treatment and medication','2025-10-21 13:09:51'),(329231,'- access to information on new and current trials','2025-10-21 13:09:51'),(329232,'- promotion of research into new treatment/medication','2025-10-21 13:09:51'),(329233,'- information exchange and collaboration between European and international PF patient associations','2025-10-21 13:09:51'),(329234,'- supporting the establishment of patient associations in countries where no such associations exist','2025-10-21 13:09:51'),(329235,'Traffic safety policy and issues related to this such as vehicle and road network safety','2025-10-21 13:09:51'),(329236,'Clean up the Internet is engaged in the European Commission\'s digital regulation agenda, including enforcement of the Digital Services Act, initiatives to counter disinformation and electoral interference, and associated policies in the realm of the regulation of social media companies','2025-10-21 13:09:52'),(329237,'European healthcare policies, drug policies, industrial development Contact with European institutions','2025-10-21 13:09:53'),(329238,'Circularity','2025-10-21 13:09:53'),(329239,'With the initiative Generation LINK: Learn, Inspire, Network, Knowledge – Transfer, YES Forum and its member organisations align with the new EU strategy, THE UNION OF SKILLS, which focuses on building skills for quality jobs and better lives, upskilling and reskilling an agile workforce, attracting, developing, and retaining talent YES Forum strongly advocates for this ambitious and comprehensive approach to EU skills policy, emphasising that young people and the social service sector are essential to its success Social sector organisations play a crucial role in this process - not only benefiting from these developments but actively shaping, implementing, and driving them forward','2025-10-21 13:09:54'),(329240,'YES Forum contributes to the EUROPEAN PILLAR OF SOCIAL RIGHTS ACTION PLAN by transforming its principles into concrete actions that benefit disadvantaged young people and the professionals who support them We play our unique role alongside our member organisations across EU Member States to help implement the Pillar of Social Rights Through our work, we actively support these collective efforts to build a fairer and more inclusive Europe','2025-10-21 13:09:54'),(329241,'By providing formal and non-formal learning, the YES Forum promotes social inclusion and active participation of young people with vulnerable background in society, thus contributing to the implementation of the European Pillar of Social Rights Action Plan through innovative and holistic education and training, including upskilling and reskilling All this with the aim to enhance youth employment, youth participation and social inclusion Especially the YES Forum focuses on four principles under the Chapter I: “Equal opportunities and access to the labour market”: education, training and life-long learning gender equality equal opportunities and active support to employment','2025-10-21 13:09:54'),(329242,'Furthermore our work resonates with THE EUROPEAN UNION (EU) YOUTH STRATEGY complementing the dual approach by mainstreaming youth issues across policy areas alongside specific youth initiatives','2025-10-21 13:09:54'),(329243,'Impact reports: https://wwwyes-forumeu/our-work/publications/','2025-10-21 13:09:54'),(329244,'- Commission Implementing Decisions for Work Programmes of Horizon Europe and FP10','2025-10-21 13:09:55'),(329245,'- Horizon Europe strategic plan 2025-2027','2025-10-21 13:09:55'),(329246,'- Commission Implementing Decision Erasmus+','2025-10-21 13:09:55'),(329247,'Human Rights, Human Rights Defenders, External Action, Foreign Policy, Women\'s Rights, LGBTI, Freedom of Association','2025-10-21 13:09:56'),(329248,'This includes Visa regulation: visa code and handbook  Human Rights Defenders Guidelines  European Parliament resolution of 16 March 2023 on the EU Guidelines on Human Rights Defenders  Financing instruments: Neighbourhood, Development and International Cooperation Instrument – Global Europe','2025-10-21 13:09:56'),(329249,'Les principaux dossiers que TEJO suit le plus sont liés aux droits linguistiques, notamment avec le Minority Safepack, et au plurilinguisme, par exemple dans le cadre de la consultation menée par la médiatrice européenne','2025-10-21 13:09:57'),(329250,'TEJO est aussi présente dans les discussions sur le Cadre Financier Pluriannuel, étant par exemple attaché à un programme Erasmus+ ambitieux et accessible à tous','2025-10-21 13:09:57'),(329251,'Enfin, le troisième grand sujet où TEJO est impliqué est le Dialogue structuré et la question des Droits des jeunes','2025-10-21 13:09:57'),(329252,'Política Agraria Común (PAC)','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329253,'Marco Financiero Plurianual (MFP)','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329254,'Estrategia de \"la Granja a la mesa\"','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329255,'Biodiversidad 2030','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329256,'AGRI: Agricultura y Desarrollo Rural','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329257,'ENVI: Cambio Climático y Sostenibilidad Medioambiental','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329258,'SANTE: Salud y Seguridad Alimentaria','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329259,'INTA: Comercio Internacional y Acuerdos Comerciales','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329260,'Innovación, Investigación y H20','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329261,'Derecho de la Competencia','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329262,'Organización Mundial del Comercio (OMC)','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329263,'Políticas de Consumo y Alimentación','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329264,'Gestión de mercados y crisis','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329265,'Observatorios europeos','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329266,'Cadena agroalimentaria','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329267,'Conferencia sobre el Futuro de Europa','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329268,'Congreso de Jóvenes Agricultores','2025-10-21 13:09:58'),(329269,'We follow work on intergenerational justice and solidarity, and on making the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) more relevant within the European Union, in particular through institutions and bodies that can play a pioneering role in the  (supra)national implementation of sustainable development Further, we facilitate cross-border policy dialogues to foster the idea of an Energy Union based on renewable energy We also follow work at the European Union in other areas of our work that include  financial stability, violence against women and girls, and disability','2025-10-21 13:10:00'),(329270,'Space and defence, EU neighborhood policy, regional policy, european defence industrial srategy (EDIS, WHITE PAPER FOR EUROPEAN DEFENCE and the ReArm EUROPE Plann/READINESS 2030, ASAP, EDIRPA)','2025-10-21 13:10:00'),(329271,'•	EU’s next long-term budget (MFF) – EU funding for competitiveness','2025-10-21 13:10:01'),(329272,'•	EU’s next long-term budget (MFF) – EU funding for civil protection, preparedness and response to crises','2025-10-21 13:10:01'),(329273,'•	EU’s next long-term budget (MFF) – EU funding for the single market, and cooperation between national authorities','2025-10-21 13:10:01'),(329274,'•	EU’s next long-term budget (MFF) – EU funding for cross-border education, training and solidarity, young people, media, culture, and creative sectors, values, and civil society','2025-10-21 13:10:01'),(329275,'•	EU’s next long-term budget (MFF) – EU funding for external action','2025-10-21 13:10:01'),(329276,'•	EU’s next long-term budget (MFF) – performance of the EU budget','2025-10-21 13:10:01'),(329277,'•	EU’s next long-term budget (MFF) – implementing EU funding with Member States and regions','2025-10-21 13:10:01'),(329278,'- European Parliament resolution of 19 January 2023 on the EU response to the protests and executions in Iran (2023/2511(RSP))','2025-10-21 13:10:02'),(329279,'- Council Implementing Decision (CFSP) 2023/1299 of 26 June 2023 implementing Decision 2011/235/CFSP concerning restrictive measures directed against certain persons and entities in view of the situation in Iran','2025-10-21 13:10:02'),(329280,'- Council Implementing Decision (CFSP) 2023/987 of 22 May 2023 implementing Decision 2011/235/CFSP concerning restrictive measures directed against certain persons and entities in view of the situation in Iran','2025-10-21 13:10:02'),(329281,'- Council Implementing Regulation (EU) 2023/846 of 24 April 2023 implementing Regulation (EU) No 359/2011 concerning restrictive measures directed against certain persons, entities and bodies in view of the situation in Iran','2025-10-21 13:10:02'),(329282,'- European Parliament resolution of 17 February 2022 on the death penalty in Iran','2025-10-21 13:10:02'),(329283,'(2022/2541(RSP))','2025-10-21 13:10:02'),(329284,'Industrial Clean Deal, European Green Deal and Fit for 55, including EU Climate Law and goals, revision of Renewable Energy Directive, Energy Taxation Directive and Fuel Quality Directive, EU Emission Trading System, CBAM as well as relevant strategies, such as EU Industry Strategy and EU Smart and Sustainable Mobility Strategy','2025-10-21 13:10:02'),(329285,'Ecodesign directive and the related Energy Labelling Directive, which mandate minimum energy efficiency requirements and require the use of labels to inform consumers The Ecodesign Regulation (EU) 547/2012 sets specific standards, such as the Minimum Efficiency Index (MEI) for rotodynamic water pumps and the Energy Efficiency Index (EEI) for glandless circulators, to phase out inefficient models These regulations ensure that new pumps placed on the EU market meet energy performance criteria, while the EPREL database provides public access to energy performance information','2025-10-21 13:10:03'),(329286,'Ecodesign Directive and the Energy Efficiency Directive (EED), mandating minimum energy efficiency requirements for motors, variable speed drives (VSDs), and integrated motor-drive systems Regulation (EU) 2019/1781, which replaced the previous 2009/2016 regulations, sets efficiency classes (eg, IE3, IE4) for motors and requires specific minimum efficiency levels, and also addresses integrated motor and VSDs and replacement motors','2025-10-21 13:10:03'),(329287,'Commission Regulation (EU) 2019/1781 laying down Ecodesign requirements for electric motors and variable speed drives (VSDs)','2025-10-21 13:10:03'),(329288,'Revisione della Direttiva sulle Energie Rinnovabili (RED II)','2025-10-21 13:10:04'),(329289,'Piano REPowerEU','2025-10-21 13:10:04'),(329290,'Comunicazione della Commissione Europea COM(2019) 640 finale, \"Green Deal Europeo\"','2025-10-21 13:10:04'),(329291,'Air Cargo related Customs and Taxation matters / Aviation Security /safety & Operations/','2025-10-21 13:10:05'),(329292,'Revisione norme quadro sulla gestione dei rifiuti (n) Pacchetto economia circolare (n) Riuso e preparazione per il riutilizzo (n) EU Strategy Sustainable Textiles (n) Norme UE sulla spedizione di rifiuti (n) Promoting the Social and Solidarity Economy for Sustainable Development (n) WFD (n) Ecodesign (n)','2025-10-21 13:10:05'),(329293,'Trade (incl EU-UK, EU-US agenda, sanctions, CBAM)','2025-10-21 13:10:06'),(329294,'Energy (incl EU Methane regulation, Hydrogen & CCS, gas markets, RED)','2025-10-21 13:10:06'),(329295,'Mobility (inc emissions standards for transportation, lower carbon fuels & feedstocks for road, aviation & shipping)','2025-10-21 13:10:06'),(329296,'Climate (incl emissions trading, carbon leakage, carbon certification & offsets, EU ETS)','2025-10-21 13:10:06'),(329297,'Chemicals (incl EU Strategy for Sustainable Chemicals, REACH)','2025-10-21 13:10:06'),(329298,'Environmental Policy (incl Air Quality, water/marine policy)','2025-10-21 13:10:06'),(329299,'Sustainable Finance & Reporting Policy (incl CSRD, CSDDD','2025-10-21 13:10:06'),(329300,'1 eIDAS-verordening 20 (Verordening (EU) 910/2014 betreffende elektronische identificatie en vertrouwensdiensten)','2025-10-21 13:10:07'),(329301,'2 Single Digital Gateway-verordening (Verordening (EU) 2018/1724 tot vaststelling van één digitaal toegangspoort)','2025-10-21 13:10:07'),(329302,'3 Europese Toegankelijkheidsrichtlijn (Richtlijn (EU) 2016/2102 inzake de toegankelijkheid van websites en mobiele applicaties van overheidsinstanties)','2025-10-21 13:10:07'),(329303,'4 Dienstenrichtlijn (Richtlijn 2006/123/EG betreffende diensten op de interne markt)','2025-10-21 13:10:07'),(329304,'5 Europe\'s Digital Decade-programma (Programma Digitaal Decennium 2030)','2025-10-21 13:10:07'),(329305,'Clust-ER Health is interested in the EU policies and strategies that are of relevance to the Health and Life Sciences sectors:','2025-10-21 13:10:08'),(329306,'- EU4Health Programme','2025-10-21 13:10:08'),(329307,'- Strategic Technologies for Europe Platform (STEP)','2025-10-21 13:10:08'),(329308,'- European Health Data Space (EHDS)','2025-10-21 13:10:08'),(329309,'- Digital Europe Programme','2025-10-21 13:10:08'),(329310,'- Future EU Life Science Strategy','2025-10-21 13:10:08'),(329311,'- Future Biotech Act','2025-10-21 13:10:08'),(329312,'Proposal for a REGULATION OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL establishing rules on support for strategic plans to be drawn up by Member States under the Common agricultural policy (CAP Strategic Plans) and financed by the European Agricultural Guarantee Fund (EAGF) and by the European Agricultural Fund for Rural Development (EAFRD) and repealing Regulation (EU) No 1305/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council and Regulation (EU) No 1307/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council','2025-10-21 13:10:09'),(329313,'COM/2018/392 final - 2018/0216 (COD)','2025-10-21 13:10:09'),(329314,'Topics around health and safety in agriculure, migrant workers in agriculture, pensions','2025-10-21 13:10:09'),(329315,'Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 13 June 2024 laying down harmonised rules on artificial intelligence and amending Regulations (EC) No 300/2008, (EU) No 167/2013, (EU) No 168/2013, (EU) 2018/858, (EU) 2018/1139 and (EU) 2019/2144 and Directives 2014/90/EU, (EU) 2016/797 and (EU) 2020/1828','2025-10-21 13:10:10'),(329316,'gesamte EU Wasserpolitik mit Wasserrahmen-RL, Grundwasser-RL, Umweltqualitätsnorm, Trinkwasser-RL, Nitrat-RL, GAP, Kreislaufwirtschaft, REACH, Strategie zum Nachhaltigen Einsatz von Pestiziden, Zero Pollution Action Plan, RL zur Wasserwiederverwendung, Inspire-RL, Taxonomie für nachhaltiges Investment, Konzessions-RL, NIS RL, RL zum Schutz kritischer Infrastruktur, Industrieemissions-RL, Wasser Resilienz Strategie, uvm','2025-10-21 13:10:11'),(329317,'Critical Raw Material Directive and related supportive programs for member states and private companies','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329318,'1	Horizon Europe & the European Research Area (ERA) Policy Agenda','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329319,'STARTS is deeply embedded within the Horizon Europe programme, particularly in its emphasis on fostering interdisciplinary, challenge-driven innovation The ERA Policy Agenda for 2022–2024 includes priorities such as “deepening the ERA through broad stakeholder engagement,” where arts-based research and creative methodologies play a role in expanding epistemologies and reaching societal actors beyond traditional R&I communities','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329320,'2	New European Bauhaus (NEB)','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329321,'The NEB initiative explicitly connects the Green Deal to culture and creativity, making it a highly relevant context for STARTS Ec(h)o The call to shape more sustainable, inclusive and beautiful ways of living requires new models of collaboration between artists, scientists, and technologists Projects under STARTS offer practical models of how this convergence can lead to actionable solutions for climate, inclusion, and digital transformation','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329322,'3	Digital Decade Policy Programme (2030)','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329323,'The EU’s Digital Decade policy aims to shape a digital transition that is human-centered, inclusive, and aligned with European values STARTS contributes to this vision by promoting critical engagement with emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence, data systems, and extended realities, through artistic inquiry These approaches serve as early warning systems, foresight tools, and ethical reflections embedded within technological design — supporting objectives related to digital skills, infrastructures, and public sector digitalisation','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329324,'4	Cultural and Creative Industries (CCIs) and the European Cultural Agenda','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329325,'The renewed European Agenda for Culture highlights the role of culture in strengthening identity, innovation, and sustainability CCIs are also a strategic priority under the Creative Europe programme and the SME Strategy for a sustainable and digital Europe STARTS Ec(h)o contributes to this by positioning artists and cultural actors as active agents of innovation, not merely recipients of technology Their inclusion in R&D ecosystems also supports fairer funding structures and new skills development, especially in underserved regions','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329326,'5	AI Act and Ethical Governance of Technology','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329327,'Although not a cultural or artistic policy per se, the AI Act and related ethical frameworks have a strong bearing on the work of STARTS Artistic residencies often engage with algorithmic systems and data governance, raising questions about bias, opacity, and social impact These artistic interventions offer unique forms of civic oversight and critique, supplementing legal approaches with cultural and experiential dimensions','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329328,'6	Green Deal and Just Transition Mechanism','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329329,'The European Green Deal is fundamentally a socio-technical challenge — not only a matter of decarbonisation, but of transforming lifestyles, values, and governance structures The Just Transition requires trust, imagination, and participation STARTS artistic residencies, through experimentation and storytelling, engage citizens emotionally and imaginatively in this transition They help to prefigure future scenarios, fostering the public understanding necessary for legitimacy and uptake of climate policies','2025-10-21 13:10:12'),(329330,'CSA Regulation (COM/2022/209), the revision of Directive 2011/93/EU, and the EU Strategy for a More Effective Fight against Child Sexual Abuse (2020–2025) We also target the Anti-Trafficking Directive revision (COM/2022/732 Directive (EU) 2024/1712), the Directive on combating violence against women (COM/2022/105), and the revision of the Victims’ Rights Directive (COM/2023/424) Complementary frameworks include the Victims’ Rights Strategy (2020–2025),  the EU Strategy on the Rights of the Child (2021–2024), the New Pact on Migration and Asylum, and the Digital Services Act (Regulation (EU) 2022/2065),Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive (2024/1760) — corporate human rights and environmental due diligence obligations in value chains , Cyber Solidarity Act (Regulation (EU) 2025/38)','2025-10-21 13:10:13'),(329331,'Animal welfare legislation (transport regulation, slaughter regulation, welfare at farm directive)','2025-10-21 13:10:14'),(329332,'Animal Health Law','2025-10-21 13:10:14'),(329333,'Equine identification','2025-10-21 13:10:14'),(329334,'Size and scope of the equine sector','2025-10-21 13:10:14'),(329335,'Responsible ownership','2025-10-21 13:10:14'),(329336,'One Welfare','2025-10-21 13:10:14'),(329337,'Working Equids','2025-10-21 13:10:14'),(329338,'Labelling (country of origin, animal welfare)','2025-10-21 13:10:14'),(329339,'ΔΗΜΟΣΙΟ ΠΑΝΕΠΙΣΤΗΜΙΑΚΟ ΙΔΡΥΜΑ ΤΗΣ ΚΥΠΡΟΥ','2025-10-21 13:10:15'),(329340,'i) Digital Single Market Strategy that strives to create a harmonized digital marketplace across EU member states','2025-10-21 13:10:16'),(329341,'ii) EU\'s Green Deal and Climate Policies that can form a comprehensive plan to establish Europe as the world\'s first climate-neutral continent','2025-10-21 13:10:16'),(329342,'iii) Digital Education Action Plan and the Digital Skills and Jobs Coalition that aim to foster a digitally competent workforce through enhanced digital literacy and targeted skills training','2025-10-21 13:10:16'),(329343,'iv) Data protection and Privacy The General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) sets the standard for safeguarding personal data, and it is essential to comply with GDPR guidelines when handling such information','2025-10-21 13:10:16'),(329344,'As a not-for-profit organisation, aligning with these legislative proposals and policies allows us to contribute to the advancement of Europe\'s digital transformation, sustainable practices, digital skills development, data protection standards, and lifelong learning opportunities','2025-10-21 13:10:16'),(329345,'EU:n TEN-politiikka, satamien ympäristöasiat, satamien turvallisuus sekä rahoitus ja avustukset','2025-10-21 13:10:16'),(329346,'Working groups for the development of health policies, pharmaceutical policies and critical medicines policies in the EU','2025-10-21 13:10:17'),(329347,'Reform of the EU pharmaceutical legislation','2025-10-21 13:10:17'),(329348,'EU public procurement legislation','2025-10-21 13:10:17'),(329349,'Směrnice EU o zelených tvrzeních','2025-10-21 13:10:18'),(329350,'Entwicklungen im Bereich Erasmus+','2025-10-21 13:10:18'),(329351,'Entwicklungen im Bereich EU-Jugendstrategie','2025-10-21 13:10:18'),(329352,'Entwicklungen im Bereich Digitale Agenda','2025-10-21 13:10:18'),(329353,'Entwickliungen im Bereich Soziales Europa','2025-10-21 13:10:18'),(329354,'Entwicklungen im Bereich Jugendgarantie','2025-10-21 13:10:18'),(329355,'Teilnahme an EU-Jugendkonferenzen','2025-10-21 13:10:18'),(329356,'Teilnahme am EU Jugenddialog','2025-10-21 13:10:18'),(329357,'Forum der Zivilgesellschaft der Östlichen Partnerschaft','2025-10-21 13:10:18'),(329358,'Our main areas of focus are the following :','2025-10-21 13:10:19'),(329359,'Market in Crypto-Assets Regulation (MiCAR) implementation and review  - Regulation - 2023/1114 - EN - EUR-Lex - European Union','2025-10-21 13:10:19'),(329360,'Digi