0)','2025-10-21 13:11:03'),(329544,'•        Increase competitiveness','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329545,'•        Strengthening the Single Market, increasing its resilience and enlargement','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329546,'•        Reduce administrative burden and simplify EU legislation','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329547,'•        Actively shaping trade policy','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329548,'•        Guarantee open strategic autonomy and security of supply','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329549,'•        Sustainable transformation','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329550,'•        Affordable and secure energy supply','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329551,'•        Feasible environmental legislation','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329552,'•        Research and innovation','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329553,'•        Secure skilled labour','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329554,'•        Sustainable public finances & Capital Markets Union','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329555,'More information: https://wwwwkoat/oe/news/agenda-eu-wko-enpdf','2025-10-21 13:11:04'),(329556,'My main objectives in terms of policy are two fold:','2025-10-21 13:11:08'),(329557,'(1)	Influencing the EU\'s research and innovation programme, Horizon Europe, particularly in terms of the dissemination of evidence generated from this programme to a wider audience both within and external to the EU','2025-10-21 13:11:08'),(329558,'(2)	 Influencing the EU’s new economic foreign policy by promoting mutually beneficial partnerships particularly in the areas of science, technology, innovation, telecommunications, energy, climate, environment, natural resources, agriculture and health','2025-10-21 13:11:08'),(329559,'And finally, utilising (1) & (2) above to support the development of more active peace promotion initiatives outside the EU as well as a stronger geopolitical positioning of the EU as a block','2025-10-21 13:11:08'),(329560,'Regulatory simplification, entrepreneurship, small businesses, international trade, online payments, platform regulation','2025-10-21 13:11:09'),(329561,'- PUBLIC PROCUREMENT STRATEGY','2025-10-21 13:11:10'),(329562,'- DIGITAL SINGLE MARKET STRATEGY','2025-10-21 13:11:10'),(329563,'- EUROPEAN DATA ECONOMY','2025-10-21 13:11:10'),(329564,'- EUROPEAN COURT OF JUSTICE','2025-10-21 13:11:10'),(329565,'- GLOBAL NETWORK ON PUBLIC PROCUREMENT','2025-10-21 13:11:10'),(329566,'- SUSTAINABLE PUBLIC PROCUREMENT','2025-10-21 13:11:10'),(329567,'- Social dialogue','2025-10-21 13:11:11'),(329568,'- Management issues','2025-10-21 13:11:11'),(329569,'- Gender equality','2025-10-21 13:11:11'),(329570,'- Sustainable development','2025-10-21 13:11:11'),(329571,'- Digital transition','2025-10-21 13:11:11'),(329572,'- Future of the European Union (activities on the Conference on the Future of the EU)','2025-10-21 13:11:11'),(329573,'Strategischer Rahmen für Gesundheit und Sicherheit am Arbeitsplatz sowie dessen weitere Umsetzung hoher Arbeitsschutzstandard Kampf gegen den Krebs Integration von Menschen mit Behinderungen Förderung von Sport und Gesundheit betriebliches Gesundheitsmanagement weitere Umsetzung der Europäischen Säule sozialer Rechte Digitalisierung im Bereich der sozialen Sicherheit Zugang zum Sozialschutz für alle Erwerbstätigen, ua Plattformökonomie Herausforderungen des demographischen Wandels und der sich wandelnden Arbeitswelt bewältigen Koordinierung der Systeme sozialer Sicherheit','2025-10-21 13:11:12'),(329574,'Kansanterveyden edistäminen Voittoa tavoittelematon ja ei-kaupallinen toimija seuraavilla aloilla: Alkoholi-, tupakka- ja huumausainepolitiikat, rahapelaaminen, terveyden edistäminen ja kansanterveys, mielenterveyden edistäminen, hyvinvointipolitiikka, elintarvikepolitiikka, ravitsemuspolitiikka, talouspolitiikka, sosiaali- ja terveyspalvelut, köyhyyden ja syrjäytymisen ehkäiseminen','2025-10-21 13:11:13'),(329575,'The organisation Latvijas Mednieku savienība (Latvian Hunters’ Association) represents the interests of Latvian hunters and promotes sustainable hunting practices, nature conservation, biodiversity management, and rural development Our activities are linked to several EU policy areas and legislative frameworks that affect hunting, wildlife management, and the sustainable use of natural resources','2025-10-21 13:11:14'),(329576,'Specifically, our organisation’s interests and interactions concern:','2025-10-21 13:11:14'),(329577,'EU Biodiversity Strategy for 2030 and related initiatives under the EU Green Deal, particularly in relation to sustainable use of wild species, management of game populations, and coexistence of conservation objectives with traditional rural activities','2025-10-21 13:11:14'),(329578,'Nature Restoration Law (COM/2022/304) and the implementation of the Birds Directive (2009/147/EC) and the Habitats Directive (92/43/EEC) — focusing on the management of species of hunting interest and their habitats','2025-10-21 13:11:14'),(329579,'Common Agricultural Policy (CAP) — especially measures under rural development and agri-environmental schemes that influence wildlife habitats and the socio-economic role of hunting in rural communities','2025-10-21 13:11:14'),(329580,'Firearms Regulation and Firearms Directive (Directive (EU) 2021/555) — concerning the lawful possession, transport, and use of hunting firearms','2025-10-21 13:11:14'),(329581,'EU Animal Health Law (Regulation (EU) 2016/429) and Food Safety legislation, particularly with regard to game meat and disease control (eg, African swine fever)','2025-10-21 13:11:14'),(329582,'EU Forest Strategy and EU Climate Policy — insofar as they affect forest and wildlife management practices','2025-10-21 13:11:14'),(329583,'Description of activities involving EU institutions:','2025-10-21 13:11:14'),(329584,'Latvijas Mednieku savienība monitors EU legislative and policy developments relevant to hunting and biodiversity, provides feedback through consultations and position papers, and participates in stakeholder dialogues, conferences, and expert groups when appropriate The organisation also cooperates with European hunting and conservation umbrella bodies (such as FACE – the European Federation for Hunting and Conservation) to represent the views and experience of Latvian hunters at EU level','2025-10-21 13:11:14'),(329585,'Our interactions with EU institutions are therefore limited to policy monitoring, information exchange, and advocacy activities aimed at promoting sustainable hunting and nature conservation consistent with EU environmental and rural development objectives','2025-10-21 13:11:14'),(329586,'Answering the Call for expressions of interest from EU/EEA/Western Balkans-based businesses to invest in the Western Balkans','2025-10-21 13:11:15'),(329587,'The company is a mission-driven sports tech organization specializing in AI-powered solutions for football scouting and player development Its core objective is to bridge the gap between grassroots talent and professional opportunities by digitizing outdated scouting systems and empowering local stakeholders with modern tools, data, and skills Through its innovative digital platform, the company enables football clubs, academies, and federations to evaluate youth players objectively and efficiently, using performance analytics, video analysis, and smart data aggregation','2025-10-21 13:11:15'),(329588,'A central focus of the company’s activities is accelerating the digital transition within the sports sector, especially in underserved and less digitally mature regions The company’s platform replaces informal, manual scouting methods with a mobile-first, cloud-based ecosystem that is fully GDPR-compliant and optimized for low-bandwidth environments This allows even rural or remote football communities in the Western Balkans to access cutting-edge technology and participate in broader talent networks By integrating local institutions—such as football academies, grassroots clubs, and NGOs—into a unified digital framework, the company fosters interoperability, transparency, and cross-border data collaboration','2025-10-21 13:11:15'),(329589,'Beyond technology deployment, the company is deeply committed to human capital development as a driver of sustainable socio-economic impact As part of its project in the Western Balkans, the company will train over 100 local coaches, scouts, and analysts in digital scouting methodologies, equipping them with relevant skills in sports data analysis, AI-assisted video review, and platform-based talent profiling These capacity-building efforts not only enhance local employment opportunities within the sports and tech sectors but also align with EU goals of empowering youth, advancing digital literacy, and increasing access to tech-driven professions','2025-10-21 13:11:15'),(329590,'The company views football as a high-impact entry point for broader digital inclusion and workforce transformation By embedding training and certification programs within its platform rollout, it ensures that local professionals are not only users but also contributors and innovators in the ecosystem These efforts are particularly crucial in regions with limited access to formal training infrastructure, where digital skilling can serve as a catalyst for both personal development and community advancement','2025-10-21 13:11:15'),(329591,'The company’s model also contributes to regional integration—another key EU objective—by establishing the first cross-border digital database of youth footballers in the Western Balkans This facilitates structured data-sharing and joint scouting efforts between Serbia, Bosnia and Herzegovina, and North Macedonia, strengthening professional mobility and regional cooperation through sport','2025-10-21 13:11:15'),(329592,'In summary, the company offers a scalable, technology-enabled solution that supports the EU’s dual goals of digital transition and human capital development Its platform reduces digital divides, equips the next generation of sports professionals with future-proof skills, and builds a replicable model that can extend into other sectors, such as education, health, and social development—contributing meaningfully to inclusive growth across the region','2025-10-21 13:11:15'),(329593,'EU Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive','2025-10-21 13:11:16'),(329594,'Regulation on deforestation-free products','2025-10-21 13:11:16'),(329595,'Conflict Minerals Regulation','2025-10-21 13:11:16'),(329596,'EU Non Financial Reporting Directive / Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive','2025-10-21 13:11:16'),(329597,'EU Action Plan on Sustainable Finance','2025-10-21 13:11:16'),(329598,'1- Proposal for a Regulation of the European Parliament and of the Council establishing the Union Customs Code and the European Union Customs Authority and repealing Regulation (EU) 952/2013','2025-10-21 13:11:19'),(329599,'Proposal for a Council Directive restructuring the Union framework taxation of energy products and electricity (recast)','2025-10-21 13:11:19'),(329600,'2- Regulation (EU) 2023/956 of the European Parliament and Council of 10 May 2023 establishing the carbon border adjustment mechanism','2025-10-21 13:11:19'),(329601,'3- Council Directive (EU) 2020/262 of 19 December 2019 laying down the general arrangements for excise duty (recast)','2025-10-21 13:11:19'),(329602,'Customs Union','2025-10-21 13:11:19'),(329603,'Excise duties','2025-10-21 13:11:19'),(329604,'Energy taxation','2025-10-21 13:11:19'),(329605,'VAT','2025-10-21 13:11:19'),(329606,'VIDA','2025-10-21 13:11:19'),(329607,'Klimapolitik, Handelspolitik, Digitalisierung, Industriepolitik, Kreislaufwirtschaft, Aus - und Weiterbildung, Soziale Unternehmensverantwortung','2025-10-21 13:11:20'),(329608,'Les principaux dossiers suivis concernent la politique de recherche (+ négociations sur Horizon Europe),  les sujets environnementaux (Green Deal, Fit for 55), les questions de politique commerciale, d\'économie circulaire, de transports et de Data','2025-10-21 13:11:21'),(329609,'- Proposal for a Framework Law for Sustainable Food Systems','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329610,'- All action points of the Farm to Fork Strategy','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329611,'- Revision of food information consumers rules (regarding FOP nutrition labelling, date-marking, green claims, geographical indications,)','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329612,'- Waste Framework directive, and all food waste related policies','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329613,'- Packaging and Packaging Waste Directive','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329614,'- Food Contact Materials Legilsation','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329615,'- EFSA’s Assessments of (Free/Added) Sugars from All Dietary Sources','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329616,'- European Commission’s Implementing Regulation on Food Origin','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329617,'- Endocrine disruptors and the draft Commission acts setting out scientific criteria for their','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329618,'determination in the context of the EU legislation on pesticides','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329619,'- Regulations reg meat denomination issue','2025-10-21 13:11:22');
INSERT INTO `proposals` VALUES (329620,'- The Commission proposal for a Regulation on \"Establishing rules on support for strategic plans to be drawn up by Member States under the Common agricultural policy (CAP Strategic Plans) and financed by the European Agricultural Guarantee Fund (EAGF) and by the European Agricultural Fund for Rural Development (EAFRD)\", repealing Regulation (EU) 1305/2013 and Regulation (EU) 1307/2013','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329621,'- Policies related to the fight against obesity and its consequences','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329622,'- EU vegan and vegetarian legislation','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329623,'- Sugar consumption reduction','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329624,'- Proposal for a Regulation on Novel Foods (nanomaterials, cloning of animals for food production)','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329625,'- The promotion of sustainable farming systems such as organic stock free farming and permaculture','2025-10-21 13:11:22'),(329626,'As National Standards Body, AFNOR essentially targets activities related to European standardization','2025-10-21 13:11:26'),(329627,'Therefore, our main priorities would include topics related to supporting the EU Single Market Strategy The following list of topics is of course not comprehensive, since legislation may be updated :','2025-10-21 13:11:26'),(329628,'-  the EU standardization regulation (Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 of the European Parliament and of the Council (https://eur-lexeuropaeu/legal-content/FR/TXT/?qid=1414068508676&uri=CELEX:32012R1025)),','2025-10-21 13:11:26'),(329629,'- the New Legislative Framework and product legislation (https://single-market-economyeceuropaeu/single-market/goods/new-legislative-framework_en),','2025-10-21 13:11:26'),(329630,'- the Digital Product Passport (https://eur-lexeuropaeu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj/eng),','2025-10-21 13:11:26'),(329631,'- the Corporate and Sustainability Reporting Directive (https://eur-lexeuropaeu/legal-content/FR/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A02022L2464-20250417)','2025-10-21 13:11:26'),(329632,'- the Omnibus IV proposal for a Directive aligning new products with the digital age (https://eceuropaeu/info/law/better-regulation/have-your-say/initiatives/14698-Omnibus-Directive-Aligning-product-legislation-with-the-digital-age_en)','2025-10-21 13:11:26'),(329633,'- Quantum technologies and Quantum Europe Strategy (https://digital-strategyeceuropaeu/en/library/quantum-europe-strategy)','2025-10-21 13:11:26'),(329634,'Regarding those, AFNOR did reply to the European Commission initiatives on the Have Your Say portal Furthermore, several meetings with national stakeholders have been organised in order to build the position for the French standardization community These workshops were also an opportunity to make stakeholders aware about the EU strategy, priorities and policies','2025-10-21 13:11:26'),(329635,'There exist European standardization organisations (CEN, CENELEC and ETSI) where AFNOR is strongly engaged AFNOR is one of the founding member of these European organisations AFNOR is member of their councils boards to contribute to governance and strategic orientations AFNOR provides, through the principle of national delegations, technical support in the technical fields','2025-10-21 13:11:26'),(329636,'JVMI\'s main policy focus is foreign policy and human rights JVMI has been invited to address a panel of the European Parliament\'s Human Rights Sub-Committee on 8 April 2025 The title of the event is: Human Rights in Iran The meeting will focus on the human rights situation in Iran JVMI will argue that human rights should become a central focus of European policy on Iran JVMI will also encourage lawmakers to adopt a resolution seeking to hold Iranian perpetrators of crimes against humanity accountable for the their crimes, including through the use of Universal Jurisdiction Officials from the European External Action Service and the UN Fact Finding Mission on Iran will also address the panel The event will be broadcast via the Parliament\'s website','2025-10-21 13:11:28'),(329637,'Tutkimus- ja innovaatiopolitiikka: Horisontti Eurooppa, aluepolitiikka: koheesiorahojen kohdentaminen, vihreä siirtymä, digitaalinen Eurooppa','2025-10-21 13:11:28'),(329638,'Η Νομοθεσία των Δημοσίων Συμβάσεων','2025-10-21 13:11:29'),(329639,'Η Νομοθεσία για την διαχείριση των Αποβλήτων που προκύπτουν από τις Εκσκαφές, τις Κατασκευές και τις Κατεδαφίσεις (ΑΕΚΚ)','2025-10-21 13:11:29'),(329640,'Οι Οδηγίες για την Κυκλική Οικονομία και την Πράσινη Συμφωνία','2025-10-21 13:11:29'),(329641,'The Centre Condorcet focusses on public-private-academic sector dialogues and on studies with an emphasis on systemic change, foresight and innovation They do not concern specific EU policy proposals,  draft regulations or directives, but broader, multi-disciplinary areas of work, such as financing transition to sustainability, new parameters for trade or neighbourhood policy, financing of green tech investments, the context of a future partnership with Africa, or new science and systemic change in agriculture or forestry, or other strategic matters in future Its work is mainly an operational transformation of research by universities or other think tanks which is tested in meetings with invited participants and summarized in its reports The Centre Condorcet has been set up to provide a legal basis for such groups which until now operated on an ad hoc basis','2025-10-21 13:11:30'),(329642,'European Commission Energy Strategy, State of the Union reports and policies- Energy and Industry, EU Trade Policy, EU 2030 Climate and Energy framework, REACH, Emissions Trading System Reform, Competition Issues','2025-10-21 13:11:31'),(329643,'le soutien au Vivre-Ensemble, a la tolérance,','2025-10-21 13:11:31'),(329644,'le respect des Droits de l\'Homme et des liberté publiques et de la liberté religieuse','2025-10-21 13:11:31'),(329645,'le respect des minorités','2025-10-21 13:11:31'),(329646,'la promotion des langues et des cultures','2025-