rung der Richtlinie (EU) 2019/1937 und der Verordnung (EU) 2023/2859 Vorschlag für eine Verordnung zur Bekämpfung von Zahlungsverzug im Geschäftsverkehr (COM(2023)0533) Richtlinienvorschlag zur Anpassung der Vorschriften über außervertragliche zivilrechtliche Haftung an künstliche Intelligenz (Richtlinie über KI-Haftung) (COM(2022) 496 final) Verordnungsvorschlag über die Sicherheit von Spielzeug und zur Aufhebung der Richtlinie 2009/48/EG (COM(2023) 462 final)','2025-10-21 13:11:35'),(329657,'o	Clean Industrial Deal, incl Action Plan for Affordable Energy, Industrial Decarbonisation Accelerator Act, Omnibus files','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329658,'o	Electrification AP, European Grids Package, energy market integration','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329659,'o	European Climate Law','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329660,'o	Security of energy markets','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329661,'o	Fit for 55 Package, incl revision of the legislation, incl RED, EED, CBAM, EMD, EPBD and eco-design','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329662,'o	Hydrogen and Gas Package and REMIT','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329663,'o	Methane emission Regulation','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329664,'o	RePowerEU Plan, incl gas emergency regulations, Regulation on security of natural gas supplies, Aggregate EU Platform, Roadmaps','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329665,'o	Energy governance, incl NECPs','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329666,'o	Industrial Carbon Management legislation, incl EU ETS and ETS2, carbon removals','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329667,'o	Net Zero Industry Act','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329668,'o	Critical Raw Materials Act','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329669,'o	Sustainable mobility (CO2 standards for vehicles, Clean corporate fleet), AFIR, STIP, ReFuelEU Aviation and Maritime, TEN-T Regulation, biofuels','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329670,'o	The Sustainable Finance (incl taxonomy)','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329671,'o	ESG, incl CSDDD, CSRD/ESRS','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329672,'o	Energy Taxation Directive','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329673,'o	Resource-related legislation (oil&gas), including stocks','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329674,'o	Trade-related issues such as anti-dumping, anti-subsidy and anti-trust decisions','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329675,'o	Energy infrastructure (ia TYNDP, TEN-E Regulation and PCI/PMI lists, Grids Package)','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329676,'o	Access to finance/support: Cohesion policy 2021-2027, Connecting Europe Facility, Green Deal Investment Plan (incl JTF, InvestEU and the EIB financing), Innovation and Moderation Funds, Recovery and Resilience Facility, Horizon Europe, Social Climate Fund, European Hydrogen Bank and MFF2028-2034','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329677,'o	State aid rules, incl CISAF','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329678,'o	Environmental legislation (incl Groundwater Directive Water Framework Directive and Strategy for Water Resilience Mining Waste Directive REACH revision IED and IEP Regulation, PFAS, Circular economy legislation, Packaging and Waste Packaging Regulation, Plastic related legislation, incl chemical recycking)','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329679,'o	Global and European LNG market development, Offshore Safety Directive, EU Offshore Energy Strategy','2025-10-21 13:11:36'),(329680,'30/12/2022 Within the  H2020 project \"DIGIPRIME\" VELTHA is developing and automated tool for the individuation of cross-sectorial and cross regional circular value chains, based on  the tool developed in the previous SCREEN project','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329681,'30/12/2022 Within the  project INTERREG EUROPE \"REPLACE\" VELTHA is advising 7 EUregion on how to integrate the tools and methodologies developed in the previous SCREEN project into their own policy instruments','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329682,'30/03/2017 Within the project SCREEN, Veltha','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329683,'works on a specific task for the establishment and operation of a \"Laboratory operations on Policies\" (Policy Lab): its aim is two-fold:','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329684,'1)	ensure that the analyses and proposals developed within the SCREEN project are discussed with EU and regional policy-makers as well as key stakeholders thereby ensuring their feasibility, relevance and effectiveness and','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329685,'2)	ensure regular exchange of information among participants so that state of the art knowledge and existing initiatives are taken into account during the implementation of the project','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329686,'The Policy Lab will be coordinated by Lazio region (coordinator of the SCREEN project) and will consist of:','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329687,'-one representative of each project partner','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329688,'-members of the SCREEN Advisory Board: ACR+, EURADA and ERRIN','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329689,'-representatives of DG REGIO, DG RTD, DG ENV, DG GROW and European Institute of Innovation and Technology','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329690,'-EASME, with the role of observer','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329691,'31/12/20162016 Veltha is following the development of the Circular Economy Package','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329692,'18/11/2013 Joint International Events Organised by VELTHA for The UNESCO Weekon Education to Sustainable Development','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329693,'28/10/2013 Veltha organizes and event in Brussels \"Supporting SMEs Research','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329694,'13/05/2011 - Position On The Green Paper On A Common Strategic Framework For EU Research And Innovation Funding (Question N°13)','2025-10-21 13:11:38'),(329695,'Regulation (EU) 2015/2283','2025-10-21 13:11:39'),(329696,'Reglamento (CE) Nº 1170/2009','2025-10-21 13:11:39'),(329697,'Directiva Europea 2022/542','2025-10-21 13:11:39'),(329698,'Regalmento (UE) 2021/2282','2025-10-21 13:11:39'),(329699,'VERORDNUNG DES EUROPÄISCHEN PARLAMENTS UND DES RATES über Qualitäts- und Sicherheitsstandards für zur Verwendung beim Menschen bestimmte Substanzen menschlichen Ursprungs und zur Aufhebung der Richtlinien 2002/98/EG und 2004/23/EG - Einreichung eines Änderungsantrages zum 892022, Aktualisierung im Februar 2023','2025-10-21 13:11:39'),(329700,'The Global Solutions Initiative envisions, proposes and evaluates policy responses to major global problems (global governance and multilateralism, climate action, digital and AI transofmration, global finance, geoeconomics and trade etc) In this, GSI generates  Policy Briefs for the policy leaders of the G20, the G7, the European Union and other international fora Decision-makers from policy-making, business and civil society contribute to the formulation of relevant policy proposals and provide a crucial bridge between the recommendations generated by the research institutions and their implementation','2025-10-21 13:11:40'),(329701,'Regulation on Forced Labour, Deforestation Regulation, Eco-design for Sustainable Products Regulation, Empowering Consumers for the Green Transition, Regulation on Substantiating Green Claims, Sustainable Food Systems, Sustainable Labelling for Food, Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive, Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive','2025-10-21 13:11:41'),(329702,'Financial market infrastructure legislation, specifically the Markets in Financial Instruments Regulation (MiFIR)','2025-10-21 13:11:41'),(329703,'• SCOHRE is an International scientific Association of independent experts on Smoking Control & Harm Reduction (established in September 2020 under the Belgian law), who seek an open and constructive dialogue to help come up with a new approach to smoking control policies','2025-10-21 13:11:42'),(329704,'• We aspire to advocate for legislation change with regard to smoking control policies to discuss with EU institutions the necessary steps for further research to create more data and evidence for legislation changes','2025-10-21 13:11:42'),(329705,'• We, at SCOHRE, believe that smoking control strategies should be reshaped to include harm reduction through alternative potentially lower risk products use, besides the traditional smoking cessation and smoking prevention measures Smoking results very often in diseases that put the life at risk eg cancer, cardiovascular disease, etc and although smokers are aware of the risk, it is very difficult to quit smokingThus, we need to define new ways and interventions to minimise the effects of smoking We, at SCOHRE, believe that harm reduction is an effective public health policy towards the right direction','2025-10-21 13:11:42'),(329706,'• Smoking cessation and prevention remain the most impactful, cost-effective interventions in medicine, but there is an ongoing discussion that limiting the negative effects of smoking can be also achieved by tobacco harm reduction','2025-10-21 13:11:42'),(329707,'• SCOHRE includes scientists from all sectors: basic science researchers, medical doctors, policy experts, behaviourists, legal experts, academics, and professionals, human rights advocates…','2025-10-21 13:11:42'),(329708,'• We need to work with EU institutions and come up with the right strategies to serve our major purpose, which is to protect the health of European citizens','2025-10-21 13:11:42'),(329709,'Proposal for a Regulation of the European Parliament and of the Council on the internal markets for renewable and natural gases and for hydrogen (Hydrogen and Gas Markets Decarbonisation Package)','2025-10-21 13:11:43'),(329710,'Recommendations on Citizen and Civil Society Organization Participation in Public Policy Development','2025-10-21 13:11:44'),(329711,'Conclusions of the European Council on Civic Space','2025-10-21 13:11:44'),(329712,'Anti-SLAPP Directive','2025-10-21 13:11:44'),(329713,'Communication from the Commission to the European Parliament, the European Council, and the Council \"Strengthening the Rule of Law in the Union - The Current Context and Possible New Initiatives\"','2025-10-21 13:11:44'),(329714,'European Rule of Law Mechanism','2025-10-21 13:11:44'),(329715,'European Pact on Migration and Asylum and Related Initiatives','2025-10-21 13:11:44'),(329716,'Belangrijkste wetgevingsvoorstellen of beleidsgebieden waarop uw organisatie zich richt:','2025-10-21 13:11:44'),(329717,'- Payments','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329718,'- E-Money','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329719,'- Dgitalisation','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329720,'- Anti-Money Laundering','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329721,'Directive 2001/18/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 12 March 2001 on the deliberate release into the environment of genetically modified organisms and repealing Council Directive 90/220/EEC','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329722,'REGULATION (EC) No 1107/2009 OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL of 21 October 2009 concerning the placing of plant protection products on the market and repealing Council Directives 79/117/EEC and 91/414/EEC','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329723,'Green Deal and Farm to Fork strategy','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329724,'Proposal for a REGULATION OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329725,'amending Regulation (EU) 2017/62','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329726,'Proposal for a REGULATION OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL on the production and marketing of plant reproductive material in the Union, amending Regulations (EU) 2016/2031, 2017/625 and 2018/848 of the European Parliament and of the Council, and repealing Council Directives 66/401/EEC, 66/402/EEC, 68/193/EEC, 2002/53/EC, 2002/54/EC, 2002/55/EC, 2002/56/EC, 2002/57/EC, 2008/72/EC and 2008/90/EC (Regulation on plant reproductive material)','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329727,'Animal nutrition and welfare','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329728,'Organics','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329729,'Carbon emissions','2025-10-21 13:11:45'),(329730,'Notice on well-functioning and sustainable local passenger transport-on-demand (taxis and PHV), Artificial Intelligence Act, Platform Work Directive, VAT rules for the digital age (VAT), Digital Services Act, Commission Delegated Regulation on EU-wide multimodal travel information services, Common European Mobility Data Space, Directive on Corporate sustainability reporting, Digital fairness act, initiative on greening corporate fleets','2025-10-21 13:11:47'),(329731,'•	The ISEFPO is a member of the Executive Committee of the North Western Waters Advisory Council (NWWAC), we are members of all four working groups and many of the focus groups and provide industry expertise to these groups','2025-10-21 13:11:47'),(329732,'•	The ISEFPO holds the Chair of Working Group 1 (Irish Sea) and the Skates and Rays Focus Group','2025-10-21 13:11:47'),(329733,'•	The ISEFPO also participates in Fisheries Improvement Meetings (FIP’s) and Technical Measures Focus Group (NWWAC)  where we lend expertise and promote new improved technical measures  We advise our members on the measures that are agreed at these meetings   Our members participate in FIP’s which improves members knowledge and encourages sustainable fisheries','2025-10-21 13:11:47'),(329734,'•	The ISEFPO participates on the Whelk Focus group, the BSA Crab Effort Meetings and other shellfish meetings at a National and European Level','2025-10-21 13:11:47'),(329735,'•	In recent years there has been a huge increase in the activity in the area of Off Shore Renewable Energy (ORE), with proposals being put forward for multiple Wind Farms in traditional fishing areas  The ISEFPO ORE/Seafood Review Group was set up to develop guidelines on interactions between the ORE Industry and the Fishing Industry, the ISEFPO has fully participated in this group and is a leading member of three subgroups   This group comprises of members from the seafood industry, Department of Marine, Department of Housing, Dept of Environment and the ORE industry','2025-10-21 13:11:47'),(329736,'•	We also are actively involved with discussions with the Department of Marine and Housing and NGO’s around the establishment of Marine Protected Areas to ensure that a sustainable fisheries and income can be maintained for our members in conjunction with these areas','2025-10-21 13:11:47'),(329737,'The ISEFPO is a member of the European group looking at the Environmental impact of bottom trawling','2025-10-21 13:11:47'),(329738,'The ISEFPO is also a member of the Market Advisory Council and disseminates information on market structures and sanitary regulations','2025-10-21 13:11:47'),(329739,'•	We also participate fully in all Department of Marine Advisory and Information forums along with other groups which we considered engagement with would be of benefit to our members eg Science Research Partnership (IFSRP), Marine Institute meetings, Bord iascaigh Mhara (BIM) workshops and training, Sea Fisheries Protection Authority (SFPA) meetings, Brexit Information meetings, All Ireland Civic Dialogue Forum, Plastics and fishing for litter Workshops, Brainstorming meetings, Harbour User’s Meetings, Onboard Fishery Observer Programme, Atypical Workers Oversight Committee,  Sumaris Project, Dept Sustainability Impact Assessment Group, SFPA Consultative Committee and Marine Survey Office Information meetings','2025-10-21 13:11:48'),(329740,'Regulation (EU) 2021/817 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 20 May 2021 establishing Erasmus+: the Union Programme for education and training, youth and sport and repealing Regulation (EU) No 1288/2013 (Text with EEA relevance)','2025-10-21 13:11:48'),(329741,'Decision (EU) 2023/936 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 10 May 2023 on a European Year of Skills (Text with EEA relevance)','2025-10-21 13:11:48'),(329742,'Olivo Foglieni ricopre le cariche di Vice Presidente Confindustria Bergamo e di Presidente della società Radiatori 2000 Spa','2025-10-21 13:11:49'),(329743,'E’ stato nominato componente del Gruppo Tecnico Energia di Confindustria Italia','2025-10-21 13:11:49'),(329744,'Si segnalano i seguenti dossier:','2025-10-21 13:11:49'),(329745,'Iniziativa su COP 26 SDG 13: Confindustria, CBI Deloitte Il progetto intende presentare un’analisi sull’impegno dell’industria italia