External Energy Engagement in a changing world (COM/2022/547 final)','2025-10-21 13:11:54'),(329788,'Regulation (EU) 2023/956 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 10 May 2023 establishing a carbon border adjustment mechanism','2025-10-21 13:11:54'),(329789,'Global Gateway Initiative in Mozambique: Our organisation is actively engaged in advancing the objectives of the Global Gateway Strategy of the European Union, particularly in the context of renewable energy infrastructure development and sustainable economic growth in Mozambique We collaborate closely with the EU Delegation to Mozambique to support the implementation of energy projects that aim to enhance access to renewable energy, particularly in rural and underserved regions These efforts align with the broader goals of the European Green Deal and the EU External Investment Plan, which seeks to promote sustainable development and investments in partner countries','2025-10-21 13:11:54'),(329790,'EU Renewable Energy and AMER Partnership: Our organisation is an active partner of the Associação Moçambicana de Energias Renováveis (AMER), a prominent Mozambican organisation dedicated to the promotion and development of renewable energy Through this collaboration, we work to influence EU policy and investment in renewable energy projects in Mozambique, aligning with the EU’s Renewable Energy Directive (RED III) (Directive (EU) 2023/2413) and the European Green Deal These policies are central to ensuring that EU investments contribute to the sustainable development of Mozambique\'s energy sector Furthermore, we advocate for the inclusion of Mozambique’s renewable energy projects within the scope of the Global Gateway Initiative, ensuring that EU-funded infrastructure projects are aligned with regional and national energy transition goals','2025-10-21 13:11:54'),(329791,'EU Renewable Energy Policy: Our organisation also works to influence the legislative framework surrounding the Renewable Energy Directive (RED III), Directive (EU) 2023/2401, which is part of the EU\'s Clean Energy for All Europeans package This directive sets binding renewable energy targets for all EU Member States and plays a critical role in shaping external energy policies and the EU’s commitment to climate action globally We advocate for increased EU support for renewable energy projects in Mozambique, aligning with the goals of the European Green Deal and EU’s Global Gateway strategy to help meet the EU\'s climate and sustainability objectives','2025-10-21 13:11:54'),(329792,'2021/0104(COD) Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive','2025-10-21 13:11:55'),(329793,'2022/0051(COD) Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence','2025-10-21 13:11:55'),(329794,'2000/2141(COS) European Community\'s development policy','2025-10-21 13:11:55'),(329795,'Matters related to development cooperation and development financing, to corporate sustainability and reporting','2025-10-21 13:11:55'),(329796,'Overall legislation related to the  Food industry and sustainable economic activities','2025-10-21 13:11:55'),(329797,'*Clean Industrial Deal','2025-10-21 13:11:56'),(329798,'*Climate Target 2040 and Industrial Carbon Management Strategy','2025-10-21 13:11:56'),(329799,'*Implementation of Green Deal, in particular: Fit for 55 proposals, Hydrogen and Decarbonised Gas Market Package, F-Gases Regulation, Greening Freight Package','2025-10-21 13:11:56'),(329800,'* Electricity Market Design','2025-10-21 13:11:56'),(329801,'* AI, Cyber Security, Gigabit Infrastructure and Data Legislation','2025-10-21 13:11:56'),(329802,'* Sustainable and intelligent Mobility Strategy','2025-10-21 13:11:56'),(329803,'* Autonomous driving','2025-10-21 13:11:56'),(329804,'* Initiatives on Urban Mobility','2025-10-21 13:11:56'),(329805,'* Technical Harmonization (urban rail)','2025-10-21 13:11:56'),(329806,'* Equality and Gender policies','2025-10-21 13:11:56'),(329807,'Tapaamisessa komissaarin kanssa 2962025 tulee Nordic Troutin edustajana 