onsumer and related amendments including the Regulation 2019/1381 on the transparency and sustainability of the EU risk assessment in the food chain and initiatives foreseen in the Farm to Fork strategy','2025-10-21 13:14:50'),(330561,'- Implementation measures linked to Regulation (EC) 1924/2006 on Nutrition &Health Claims and any relevant initiatives foreseen in the Farm to Fork strategy','2025-10-21 13:14:50'),(330562,'- Implementation measures in the area of public health and nutrition under Article168 of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union','2025-10-21 13:14:50'),(330563,'- Implementation of the Vision for Agriculture and Food, including the yearly Food Dialogue','2025-10-21 13:14:50'),(330564,'Protein strategy','2025-10-21 13:14:54'),(330565,'EU Funds and Programmes: Advocate for dedicated funding and support mechanisms for social economy enterprises in Greece through EU funding programmes such as the Just Transition Fund, European Social Fund, European Regional Development Fund, and InvestEU','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330566,'Public Procurement: Advocate for the inclusion of social and environmental criteria in public procurement processes to promote the participation of social economy enterprises in public contracts','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330567,'Social Business Initiative: Engage with the European Commission to ensure the effective implementation of the Social Business Initiative, including the promotion of social entrepreneurship and access to finance for social economy enterprises','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330568,'European Pillar of Social Rights: Advocate for the integration of social economy principles and practices into the implementation of the European Pillar of Social Rights, particularly in areas such as fair working conditions, social protection, and access to quality healthcare and education','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330569,'Circular Economy: Promote the role of social economy enterprises in the transition towards a circular economy by advocating for supportive policies, funding, and capacity-building initiatives','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330570,'Social Innovation: Advocate for the recognition and support of social innovation initiatives in the EU, which can foster the development of social economy enterprises and their ability to address societal challenges','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330571,'Social Inclusion and Poverty Reduction: Advocate for EU policies and initiatives that aim to tackle social exclusion, poverty, and unemployment, ensuring that social economy enterprises are recognized as key actors in these efforts','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330572,'Social Investment: Advocate for EU policies and instruments that promote social investment and impact finance, facilitating access to funding and support for social economy enterprises','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330573,'Sustainable Development Goals: Promote the alignment of EU policies and initiatives with the United Nations\' Sustainable Development Goals, advocating for the integration of social economy principles and practices in the achievement of these goals','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330574,'Cross-Sectoral Collaboration: Advocate for the promotion of cross-sectoral collaboration between social economy enterprises, traditional businesses, public authorities, and civil society organizations to foster innovation, social cohesion, and sustainable development','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330575,'Energy Production and Renewables: Promote the role of social economy enterprises in the renewable energy sector and advocate for policies that facilitate their participation in energy production projects','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330576,'Energy Efficiency: Advocate for EU policies and funding programs that support energy efficiency measures, such as energy-efficient building renovations and energy-saving technologies Promote the participation of social economy enterprises in the implementation of such initiatives, as they can contribute to job creation, social inclusion, and environmental sustainability','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330577,'Just and Sustainable Transition Strategy: Advocate for the inclusion of social economy principles and practices in the EU\'s Just and Sustainable Transition Strategy Ensure that the needs and potential of social economy enterprises are recognized and supported in the transition to a climate-neutral and sustainable economy','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330578,'Green Jobs and Skills: Advocate for EU policies and programs that promote the creation of green jobs and the development of skills needed in the renewable energy and energy efficiency sectors Highlight the role of social economy enterprises in providing quality employment opportunities and supporting the upskilling and reskilling of workers in these sectors','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330579,'Community Energy Cooperatives: Advocate for the recognition and support of community energy cooperatives within the EU\'s energy policy framework Promote the role of social economy enterprises in fostering citizen participation, local ownership, and democratic decision-making in energy production and distribution','2025-10-21 13:14:55'),(330580,'1 Regulamentul (UE) nr 1151/2012 al Parlamentului European și al Consiliului din 21 noiembrie 2012 privind sistemele din domeniul calității produselor agricole și alimentare','2025-10-21 13:14:56'),(330581,'2 Regulamentul de punere în aplicare (UE) nr 1085/2011 al Comisiei din 27 octombrie 2011 de modificare a Regulamentului (CE) nr 501/2008 de stabilire a normelor de aplicare a Regulamentului (CE) nr 3/2008 al Consiliului privind acțiunile de informare și promovare pentru produsele agricole pe piața internă și în țările terțe','2025-10-21 13:14:56'),(330582,'3 Regulamentul (UE) nr 1144/2014 al Parlamentului European și al Consiliului din 22 octombrie 2014 privind acțiunile de informare și promovare referitoare la produsele agricole puse în aplicare pe piața internă și în țările terțe și de abrogare a Regulamentului (CE) nr 3/2008 al Consiliului','2025-10-21 13:14:56'),(330583,'4 Regulamentul (UE) nr 1305/2013 al Parlamentului European și al Consiliului din 17 decembrie 2013 privind sprijinul pentru dezvoltare rurală acordat din Fondul european agricol pentru dezvoltare rurală (FEADR) și de abrogare a Regulamentului (CE) nr 1698/2005 al Consiliului','2025-10-21 13:14:56'),(330584,'5Regulamentul (UE) nr 1307/2013 al Parlamentului European și al Consiliului din 17 decembrie 2013 de stabilire a unor norme privind plățile directe acordate fermierilor prin scheme de sprijin în cadrul politicii agricole comune și de abrogare a Regulamentului (CE) nr 637/2008 al Consiliului și a Regulamentului (CE) nr 73/2009 al Consiliului','2025-10-21 13:14:56'),(330585,'6 Regulamentul (CE) nr 1333/2008 al Parlamentului European și al Consiliului din 16 decembrie 2008 privind aditivii alimentari (Text cu relevanță pentru SEE)','2025-10-21 13:14:56'),(330586,'Renoon focuses on key EU legislative proposals shaping the future of sustainability and transparency in the fashion industry Our main targets include the Digital Product Passport (DPP) for textiles, a core requirement under the Ecodesign for Sustainable Products Regulation (ESPR), which mandates product-level traceability and environmental impact disclosure We also address the Green Claims Directive, ensuring accurate and verifiable sustainability communications, and the Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive (CSDDD), which holds companies accountable for their supply chains By aligning our Digital Product Passport solution with these policies, we help brands navigate compliance, enhance transparency, and contribute to a more sustainable fashion ecosystem','2025-10-21 13:14:56'),(330587,'Regulation of the European Parliament and of the Council on establishing a framework of measures for strengthening Europe’s net-zero technology products manufacturing ecosystem (Net Zero Industry Act) Industrial Carbon Management Strategy Carbon Removals Framework Industrial Carbon Management','2025-10-21 13:14:58'),(330588,'Hydrogen and Gas Markets Decarbonisation Package','2025-10-21 13:14:58'),(330589,'RED III','2025-10-21 13:14:58'),(330590,'European Hydrogen Bank','2025-10-21 13:14:58'),(330591,'EU Global Gateway','2025-10-21 13:14:58'),(330592,'To date, Fad Juventud is an active communication actor in the Spanish society We advocate for a better development of young people through sociological reserarch and the implementation of social awareness campaings, educational programs, and international cooperation programs in Latinoamerica All activities have a great impact in society','2025-10-21 13:14:59'),(330593,'The Fad Juventud is commited to make youth:','2025-10-21 13:14:59'),(330594,'Less vulnerable to risks','2025-10-21 13:14:59'),(330595,'More emotionally healthy and balanced','2025-10-21 13:14:59'),(330596,'More visible, active and vocal','2025-10-21 13:14:59'),(330597,'More prepared for digital citizenship and with more job opportunities','2025-10-21 13:14:59'),(330598,'More proactive in their learning and with greater critical capacity','2025-10-21 13:14:59'),(330599,'More committed to citizenship and equality','2025-10-21 13:15:00'),(330600,'More integrated in contexts free of violence','2025-10-21 13:15:00'),(330601,'Unser Unternehmen beobachtet die Entwicklung der nachhaltigen Kraftstoffe, Stromspeicherung, Re-Industrialisierung und Klimaschutz sowie die Entwicklung der Dekarbonisierungsstrategie entsprechend der Road-Map 2050','2025-10-21 13:15:00'),(330602,'Biobes shpk engages with EU legislation and policies relevant to the production, certification, and export of organic and wild-collected medicinal and aromatic plants The key EU policies and legislative frameworks targeted include:','2025-10-21 13:15:01'),(330603,'Regulation (EU) 2018/848 on organic production and labelling of organic products','2025-10-21 13:15:01'),(330604,'EU Biodiversity Strategy for 2030, especially regarding sustainable