REGULATION (EU) 2022/2554 OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL of 14 December 2022 on digital operational resilience for the financial sector and amending Regulations (EC) No 1060/2009, (EU) No 648/2012, (EU) No 600/2014, (EU) No 909/2014 and (EU) 2016/1011','2025-10-21 13:15:10'),(330663,'Proposal for a DIRECTIVE OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL amending Directives (EU) 2009/65/EC, 2009/138/EC, 2011/61/EU, 2014/65/EU and (EU) 2016/97 as regards the Union retail investor protection rules','2025-10-21 13:15:10'),(330664,'Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 25 November 2009 on the taking-up and pursuit of the business of Insurance and Reinsurance (Solvency II)','2025-10-21 13:15:10'),(330665,'Proposal for a REGULATION OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL amending Regulation (EU) 2017/2402 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 12 December 2017 laying down a general framework for securitisation and creating a specific framework for simple, transparent and standardised securitisation','2025-10-21 13:15:10'),(330666,'Proposal for a REGULATION OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL amending Regulation (EU) No 575/2013 on prudential requirements for credit institutions as regards requirements for securitisation exposures','2025-10-21 13:15:10'),(330667,'We have a singular goal: having each European farmer farming in harmony with nature','2025-10-21 13:15:13'),(330668,'To realise this vision, we believe the CAP (the Common Agricultural Policy of the EU) structure needs to change from action-based to result-based payments centred on climate measures Furthermore, we see the key acceleration and synthesising role in this transition for the private agricultural carbon payment programs and connecting those with the CAP','2025-10-21 13:15:13'),(330669,'This is why our key area of focus is the CAP and its evolution in the 2028-2034 budget We advocate for the continuation of the separate budget for the CAP, as well as its transition towards result-based payments','2025-10-21 13:15:13'),(330670,'Regulation on standards of quality and safety for substances of human origin intended for human application','2025-10-21 13:15:14'),(330671,'The New Mobility Association (PSNM - Polskie Stowarzyszenie Nowej Mobilności) is involved and aims at contributing to the following areas of EU legislation and policy:','2025-10-21 13:15:15'),(330672,'- The European Green Deal - PSNM aims at developing the zero emission, electric road transport in Poland and the CEE region, hence it is crucial for the organization to take up advocacy work in order to represent the electromobility sector in Poland in the process of shaping the policies related to implementing the European Geen Deal','2025-10-21 13:15:15'),(330673,'- Fit for 55 legislation package - PSNM aims at developing the zero emission, electric road transport in Poland and the CEE region, hence it is crucial for the organization to take up advocacy work in order to represent the electromobility sector in Poland in the process of shaping the policies related to implementing the legislation acts proposed within the Fit for 55 proposal This pertains especially to the Regulation on the deployment of the alternative fuels\' infrastructure, but also to other acts regulating building energy efficiency','2025-10-21 13:15:15'),(330674,'- Battery regulations - as a representative of the Polish market, now hosting the largest manufacturing site in the EU and one of the largest in the world, PSNM focuses on developing this market, with efforts aligned with the Association\'s goals Furthermore, PSNM aims at developing the R&D and innovative thought in Poland, to make the market a battery competence hub, hence PSNM contributions to the legislation and policy on this topic are crucial for PSNM\'s Members','2025-10-21 13:15:15'),(330675,'- Electromobility - all area of legislation and policy concerning the electromobility market','2025-10-21 13:15:15'),(330676,'- New Mobility - all area of legislation and policy concerning zero emission road transport, including alternative fuels and hydrogen mobility','2025-10-21 13:15:15'),(330677,'- NZIA - all areas relate to the development of the EU global competitiveness and the CEE role in driving this process are also of great significance for PSNM','2025-10-21 13:15:15'),(330678,'Pave the way for a green transitions within the industry','2025-10-21 13:15:16'),(330679,'European Green Deal: Commission proposes to boost renovation and decarbonisation of buildings','2025-10-21 13:15:16'),(330680,'Proposed Regulation to address distortions caused by foreign subsidies in the Single Market','2025-10-21 13:15:16'),(330681,'1 EU Taxonomy for Sustainable Activities','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330682,'Objective: Defines which economic activities can be considered environmentally sustainable','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330683,'Why it matters for SNN:','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330684,'Nuclear is conditionally included, and this supports access to green finance and improves investor confidence','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330685,'SNN advocates for stable inclusion of nuclear as sustainable to finance projects like SMRs, Unit 1 refurbishment, and Units 3&4','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330686,'2 Euratom Treaty & Related Legislation','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330687,'Objective: Regulates nuclear safety, radiation protection, safeguards, and nuclear fuel supply','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330688,'Ensures compliance for all nuclear projects','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330689,'Relevant in diversifying fuel supply and reducing dependency on Russia (eg, switch to Western fuel for CANDU reactors)','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330690,'Key in accessing Euratom loans','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330691,'3 State Aid Guidelines (CEEAG + Art 107 TFEU)','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330692,'Objective: Controls how governments support energy projects to ensure fair competition','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330693,'SNN\'s major projects