onal partnerships','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330713,'Strengthens SNN’s role in regional energy security (eg, Moldova exports)','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330714,'Supports EU backing for Romanian nuclear as a regional decarbonization anchor','2025-10-21 13:15:17'),(330715,'The EU Omnibus Package','2025-10-21 13:15:18'),(330716,'EU tax decluttering and simplification','2025-10-21 13:15:18'),(330717,'Supply Chain Initiative and Commercial Practices','2025-10-21 13:15:19'),(330718,'Circular Economy / Food Waste','2025-10-21 13:15:19'),(330719,'payment','2025-10-21 13:15:19'),(330720,'ERIC ha seguito lo sviluppo di quei Regolamenti, Leggi, Direttive, Comunicazioni e politiche dell\'UE in materia di sostanze chimiche In particolare ERIC ha seguito:','2025-10-21 13:15:20'),(330721,'a) Il regolamento (CE) n 1272/2008 relativo alla classificazione, all\'etichettatura e all\'imballaggio di sostanze e miscele (CLP), è stato adottato nel 2008 allo scopo di allineare il sistema dell\'UE al sistema mondiale armonizzato delle Nazioni Unite (GHS, Globally Harmonized System)','2025-10-21 13:15:20'),(330722,'b) Il regolamento (CE) n 834/2007 del Consiglio relativo alla produzione biologica e all’etichettatura dei prodotti biologici','2025-10-21 13:15:20'),(330723,'c) La direttiva Energie rinnovabili, adottata mediante codecisione il 23 aprile 2009 (direttiva 2009/28/CE recante abrogazione delle direttive 2001/77/CE e 2003/30/CE)','2025-10-21 13:15:20'),(330724,'d) La comunicazione del 6 giugno 2012 dal titolo «Energie rinnovabili: un ruolo di primo piano nel mercato energetico europeo» (COM(2012) 0271)','2025-10-21 13:15:20'),(330725,'e) La comunicazione del febbraio 2010  con i criteri non vincolanti di sostenibilità per le biomasse (COM(2010) 0011)','2025-10-21 13:15:20'),(330726,'f) Il documento COM (2016) 767 finale del 30112016 e la seguente Proposal for a DIRECTIVE OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL on the promotion of the use of energy from renewable sources','2025-10-21 13:15:20'),(330727,'Higher Education, Education & Research','2025-10-21 13:15:20'),(330728,'Forum Odbiorców Energii Elektrycznej i Gazu (FOEEiG) koncentruje się na kluczowych obszarach polityki energetycznej Unii Europejskiej, które mają wpływ na interesy odbiorców energii, w tym dużych odbiorców przemysłowych Do głównych obszarów zainteresowania należą: Polityka energetyczna i dekarbonizacja: Forum monitoruje i angażuje się w procesy legislacyjne związane z realizacją celów polityki klimatyczno-energetycznej Unii Europejskiej, w tym Pakietu \"Gotowi na 55\", który ma na celu osiągnięcie neutralności klimatycznej do 2050 roku Ważnym elementem jest analiza wpływu tych regulacji na koszty energii elektrycznej i gazu dla odbiorców przemysłowych  Rynek energii elektrycznej i gazu: Istotnym obszarem zainteresowania FOEEiG jest reforma europejskiego rynku energii, w tym regulacje dotyczące mechanizmów rynkowych, takich jak kształtowanie cen energii, dostęp do sieci oraz wsparcie  w związku z rosnącymi kosztami energii Forum angażuje się również w konsultacje dotyczące przyszłości rynku wewnętrznego energii','2025-10-21 13:15:21'),(330729,'Bezpieczeństwo dostaw energii: Forum uczestniczy w debatach dotyczących polityki bezpieczeństwa dostaw energii elektrycznej i gazu, w tym w zakresie projektów transgranicznych infrastruktury energetycznej, zwiększania odporności systemów energetycznych oraz polityki magazynowania gazu i energii','2025-10-21 13:15:21'),(330730,'Zrównoważona transformacja energetyczna: Forum koncentruje się na aspektach związanych z transformacją sektora energetycznego, w tym na wdrażaniu technologii niskoemisyjnych oraz efektywności energetycznej','2025-10-21 13:15:21'),(330731,'Polityka cenowa i konkurencyjność: Forum analizuje inicjatywy dotyczące cen energii oraz wpływu polityki energetycznej UE na konkurencyjność przemysłu europejskiego, ze szczególnym uwzględnieniem kosztów dla dużych odbiorców energii','2025-10-21 13:15:21'),(330732,'Within the 3 main EU institutions, follow and communicate about the following policies: Foreign and Security, Human Rights in general and Freedom of Religion or Belief in particular Youth, Education and Culture Neighborhood Development Emergency and Humanitarian Aid Home Security (migration issues in particular) International Trade','2025-10-21 13:15:22'),(330733,'Since ACN funds projects in most all countries in the world, it is important to follow the different policy aspects of the relation of the EU with the country where the projects are taking place In the last few years, the resurgence of the transcontinental caliphate in sub-Saharan Africa, the support to Lebanon, Syria and Iraq, and the cases of abduction and rape of women and girls from religious minorities have been a central area of concern, but nevertheless petitions of support from the rest of the world continue being tended to','2025-10-21 13:15:22'),(330734,'Missing Children Europe advocates for holistic and integrated child protection systems that respect the rights of children and responds to the needs of children (at risk of) going missing across Europe Missing Children Europe actively follows all EU files that affect this priority, with a particular emphasis on the following EU legislations and policy frameworks:','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330735,'EU Strategy on the rights of the child','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330736,'Recommendation on developing and strengthening integrated child protection systems in the best interests of the child','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330737,'EU Pact on Migration and Asylum','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330738,'EU Directive on preventing and combating trafficking in human beings and protecting its victims','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330739,'Directive on combating the sexual abuse and sexual exploitation of children and child pornography','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330740,'Victim Rights Directive','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330741,'EU Strategy on Victims\' Rights','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330742,'Regulation on a temporary derogation from certain provisions of Directive 2002/58/EC as regards the use of technologies by providers of number-independent interpersonal communications services for the processing of personal and other data for the purpose of combating online child sexual abuse','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330743,'European Electronic Communications Code (Recast) directive','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330744,'EU Strategy for a more effective fight against child sexual abuse','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330745,'Directive on the right to family reunification','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330746,'Regulation on the establishment, operation and use of the second-generation Schengen Information System (SIS II)','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330747,'Regulation concerning jurisdiction and the recognition and enforcement of judgments in matrimonial matters and the matters of parental responsibility','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330748,'Directive on certain aspects of mediation in civil and commercial matters (Directive 2008/52)','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330749,'Proposal for a regulation on the digitalisation of judicial cooperation and access to justice in cross-border civil, commercial and criminal matters, and amending certain acts in the field of judicial cooperation','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330750,'EU Strategy on the Training of Justice Professionals','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330751,'EU Strategy for LGBTIQ Equality','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330752,'EU Strategy for gender equality','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330753,'EU Strategy for the rights of persons with disabilities','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330754,'EU Roma strategic framework for equality, inclusion and participation','2025-10-21 13:15:23'),(330755,'Principal policy areas for EATiP relate to research & innovation aspects concerning: European aquaculture, Bioeconomy, Circular economy & Blue Growth  This extends to food systems, aquatic foods and environmental interactions between aquaculture & the aquatic environment','2025-10-21 13:15:24'),(330756,'Principal areas of EC engagement include: Horizon Europe Framework Programme (specifically Cluster 6), EU Mission Ocean,Blue Forum, European Partnerships, specifically Blue Economy, Food Systems & Animal Health and Welfare','2025-10-21 13:15:24'),(330757,'As of November 2023, EATiP is responsible for leading (in association with Mirror Platform Pole Aquimer and the Hauts de France Region) a Thematic Smart Specialisation Platform for Smart Circular Aquaculture','2025-10-21 13:15:24'),(330758,'Further areas of interest include aspects of food safety, consumer issues, regional economic development, data use, precision farming, nature based solutions & environment services offered through aquaculture – such as habitat restoration & improved biodiversity  EATiP has collaborated with the EC in relation to aquaculture aspects of Copernicus & EMODnet and is engaging on work relating to the DTO','2025-10-21 13:15:24'),(330759,'EATiP has an interest in relevant Structural Funds (EMFAF) & Blue Invest in addition to regional cooperation (S3 Blue Economy Platform Development)','2025-10-21 13:15:24'),(330760,'EATiP engages on international collaboration activities with regard to promoting sustainable aquaculture','2025-10-21 13:15:24'),(330761,'EATiP is proactively engaging on supporting ambitions related to research & innovation contained with the Sustainable Guidelines for a European Aquaculture to 2030 (COM 2021 236 Final) & a Sustainable Blue Economy in the EU (COM 2021 240 Final) including in supporting the DG MARE / CINEA tender to deliver the Aquaculture Assistance Mechanism','2025-10-21 13:15:24'),(330762,'Policy initiatives relevant to EATiP include the Green Deal, Farm to Form Strategy, Food 2030, EU Algae Strategy, Common Fisheries Policy, Water Framework Directive, Marine Strategy Framework Directive, Marine Spatial Planning and other policies that affect water use, planning and site licensing','2025-10-21 13:15:24'),(330763,'EATiP is also concerned with issues relating to education, knowledge transfer and skills development in relation to aquaculture and the aquaculture value chain','2025-10-21 13:15:24'),(330764,'EATiP is currently a project partner for the AQUAEXCEL 30, OLAMUR & AQUAPHOENIX projects and sits on the Advisory Board of a number of further research projects and panels','2025-10-21 13:15:24'),(330765,'EATiP participates in the Aquaculture Advisory Council and SCAR Fish Committees','2025-10-21 13:15:24'),(330766,'Οικονομική και κοινωνική πολιτική, Κοινωνικός διάλογος - κοινωνικοί εταίροι, Μικρομεσαίες επιχειρήσεις, οικονομική ανάπτυξη - μεγέθυνση, Καινοτομία, Συνοχή, Κατάρτιση, Περιβάλλον, Μετανάστευση, Πνευματική και διανοητική ιδιοκτησία, Υγιεινή και ασφάλεια στο χώρο εργασίας, Ρυθμιστικό πλαίσιο, Κανόνες αγοράς, Παρεμπόριο, Απάτη, Ισότητα των φύλων, Ίσες ευκαιρίες πρόσβασης στην αγορά, Ιατρική της εργασίας','2025-10-21 13:15:25'),(330767,'EU initiatives related to quality and effective apprenticeships and work-based learning (Advisory Committee for Vocational Training - ACVT)','2025-10-21 13:15:26'),(330768,'As an affiliated organization, UGS NEZAVISNOST participate in defining European Trade Union Confederation (ETUC) priorities and policy making, their implementation and monitoring on the national level, in the different areas related to Trade Union priorities','2025-10-21 13:15:26'),(330769,'Directive on improving working conditions in platform work','2025-10-21 13:15:26'),(330770,'Initiatieven met betrekking tot de financiële sector in Europa Kapitaalmarktunie, bankregels (CRD/CRR), beleggingsregels (MiFID, UCITS, AIFMD), strategie voor duurzame financiering (SFDR, TR, CSRD, CSDDD)','2025-10-21 13:15:27'),(330771,'Brain health and innovation proposals and policies','2025-10-21 13:15:28'),(330772,'EU pharma legislation','2025-10-21 13:15:28'),(330773,'Urban Waste Water Directive','2025-10-21 13:15:28'),(330774,'Other','2025-10-21 13:15:28'),(330775,'The Cyprus Shipping Chamber follows all legislative, t