ion','2025-10-21 13:17:01'),(331112,'EU Biodiversity Strategy 2030','2025-10-21 13:17:01'),(331113,'- EU external aviation policy','2025-10-21 13:17:02'),(331114,'- Emission trading scheme','2025-10-21 13:17:02'),(331115,'- Regulation 261/2004','2025-10-21 13:17:02'),(331116,'- Regulation 712/2019','2025-10-21 13:17:02'),(331117,'- Aviation Strategy','2025-10-21 13:17:02'),(331118,'- Employment rights','2025-10-21 13:17:02'),(331119,'- EASA Basic Regulation','2025-10-21 13:17:02'),(331120,'- Revision of Regulation 1008/2008','2025-10-21 13:17:02'),(331121,'- Airport charges (or Directive 2009/12/EC)','2025-10-21 13:17:02'),(331122,'- Regulation 95/93','2025-10-21 13:17:02'),(331123,'EU employment and social policies','2025-10-21 13:17:03'),(331124,'The European Education Policy and the European Skills Agenda in the European Automotive Ecosystem','2025-10-21 13:17:03'),(331125,'Skills agenda, competitiveness and Green Deal implementation','2025-10-21 13:17:03'),(331126,'ELFA concentrates on cross-border market practice and regulatory issues affecting the buyside because we have a pan-European focus Main EU initiatives, policies and legislative files currently followed include (list not exhaustive): Securitisation Regulation, Market Abuse Regulation (MAR), Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) Directive, UCITS Eligible Assets Directive, Regulation on Credit Rating Agencies (CRA), Capital Markets Union (CMU), Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive (CSRD), Sustainable Finance Disclosure Regulation (SFDR), Alternative Investment Fund Managers Directive (AIFMD), Markets in Financial Instruments Directive II (MiFID II), Corporate Insolvency Law Harmonisation, EU Green Taxonomy, Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive and Green Bonds','2025-10-21 13:17:04'),(331127,'EU Space Programme: NorthStar Earth & Space will seek to influence the EU Space Programme to promote the interests of the European space sector, including the SSA market By actively participating in the formulation of this legislation, NorthStar aims to ensure that the EU Space Programme allocates adequate resources and support for the development and enhancement of SSA capabilities This includes fostering collaboration among EU member states and stakeholders, promoting data sharing and information exchange, and facilitating the integration of SSA technologies and services into the broader space infrastructure','2025-10-21 13:17:05'),(331128,'EU Space Strategy for Security and Defence: NorthStar Earth & Space recognizes the vital role of SSA in space-based security and defense By influencing the EU Space Strategy for Security and Defence, the organization aims to advocate for the integration of advanced SSA technologies, such as space-based sensors, data analytics, and space traffic management systems This involvement will contribute to improving Europe\'s situational awareness, enhancing space surveillance capabilities, and bolstering the security and defense of European space assets and infrastructure','2025-10-21 13:17:05'),(331129,'EU Strategy for Security & Defence: NorthStar Earth & Space will engage with the EU Strategy for Security & Defence to ensure that SSA-related aspects receive due attention The organization aims to advocate for the inclusion of SSA as a critical component of Europe\'s security and defense framework NorthStar seeks to contribute to the development of comprehensive and robust SSA policies and initiatives','2025-10-21 13:17:05'),(331130,'Future Proposal for EU Space Law: NorthStar Earth & Space aims to influence the future proposal for EU Space Law to address the evolving needs of the SSA market The organization will advocate for regulatory frameworks that support the growth and innovation of SSA technologies and services This includes considerations such as data sharing mechanisms, standardization of SSA practices, liability and insurance frameworks, and international cooperation in SSA efforts By actively participating in the law-making process, NorthStar aims to shape a legal framework that fosters the sustainable development and utilization of SSA capabilities in Europe','2025-10-21 13:17:05'),(331131,'- Charging infrastructure deployment','2025-10-21 13:17:06'),(331132,'Kommunikáció, média','2025-10-21 13:17:06'),(331133,'eIDAS and eIDAS 2 - Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and subsequent changes including Digital Wallets as part of EU Digital Identity Framework','2025-10-21 13:17:07'),(331134,'International interoperability and cooperation','2025-10-21 13:17:07'),(331135,'Información financiera y auditoría','2025-10-21 13:17:08'),(331136,'Finanzas sostenibles, incluidos bonos verdes','2025-10-21 13:17:08'),(331137,'Información corporativa en materia de sostenibilidad y su verificación (CSRD), incluidas las normas europeas de información sobre sostenibilidad (ESRS)','2025-10-21 13:17:08'),(331138,'Directiva sobre diligencia debida','2025-10-21 13:17:08'),(331139,'Gobierno corporativo','2025-10-21 13:17:08'),(331140,'Blanqueo de capitales','2025-10-21 13:17:08'),(331141,'Servicios financieros','2025-10-21 13:17:08'),(331142,'Ética profesional','2025-10-21 13:17:08'),(331143,'Auditoría del sector público','2025-10-21 13:17:08'),(331144,'Política sobre PYME','2025-10-21 13:17:08'),(331145,'AES is in contact with National Governments, Regulatory Authorities and Public Bodies on a number of energy-related issues and engages in consultations at both national and European level on environmental and market deregulation issues and on issues concerning the design, competition, structure and operation of the energy market at European and international level:','2025-10-21 13:17:08'),(331146,'EU-Japan Economic Partnership Agreement','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331147,'Forced Labour Products Ban Regulation','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331148,'EU Deforestation-Free Products Regulation (EUDR)','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331149,'Foreign Subsidies Regulation (FSR)','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331150,'Chemicals Strategy & REACH Revision','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331151,'Packaging & Packaging Waste Regulation','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331152,'Delegated Acts on RFNBOs','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331153,'Emissions Trading System (ETS)','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331154,'Industrial Carbon Management Strategy','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331155,'ReFuelEU Aviation Regulation','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331156,'FuelEU Maritime Regulation','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331157,'Delegated Act on Low-Carbon Hydrogen','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331158,'State Aid & Important Projects of Common European Interest','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331159,'Forbidden Stories does not target policies or legislation, and instead works in defense of media freedom through its investigative journalism activities The following pieces of EU legislation and regulations are however of relevance for Forbidden Stories\' work:','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331160,'- European Data Strategy','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331161,'- Recommendation on the protection, safety and empowerment of journalists','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331162,'- European Media and Audiovisual Action Plan','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331163,'- European Democracy Action Plan','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331164,'- European Democracy Shield','2025-10-21 13:17:10'),(331165,'Competition, taxation and economic policy','2025-10-21 13:17:11'),(331166,'Foreign relations and security','2025-10-21 13:17:11'),(331167,'Education and R&D policy','2025-10-21 13:17:11'),(331168,'EFCC is currently focusing on policy issues related to the Green Deal, Clean Industrial Deal, the Chemicals Strategy for Sustainability (CSS) and the Implementation of the Construction Products Regulation (CPR) In this context EFCC addresses products stewardship as well as the implementation of REACH, Classification, Labelling and Packaging (CLP) and the Chemicals Strategy for Sustainability)','2025-10-21 13:17:12'),(331169,'Moreover, EFCC actively contributes to the EU Green Deal and its supporting circular economy principles in Europe as well as the Chemicals Strategy for Sustainability and follows, and contributes to, developments regarding chemicals, polymers as well as construction materials','2025-10-21 13:17:12'),(331170,'In addition, EFCC is a partner in the HORIZON Programme, called IRISS, the InteRnatIonal ecoSystem for Safe and Sustainable by design EFCC represents the construction sector in this programme','2025-10-21 13:17:12'),(331171,'Proposal for a regulation on a Single Market for Digital Services (Digital Services Act)','2025-10-21 13:17:13'),(331172,'Reducing bureaucracy and promoting German SMEs and the startup landscape','2025-10-21 13:17:13'),(331173,'Easier access to capital and lower thresholds for investing in startups','2025-10-21 13:17:13'),(331174,'Support for innovation and patents','2025-10-21 13:17:13'),(331175,'The newly established NAVI conducts academic research and analysis that contributes to the global debate on peace, democracy, and security from the perspective of NATO-EU relations, in particular on the following topics','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331176,'1 NATO-The EU Relations','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331177,'2 The European Cyber Resilience Act','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331178,'4 The Critical Entities Resilience Directive (CER)','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331179,'8 The European Chips Act','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331180,'9 The European Data Act','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331181,'10 European Data Governance Act (DGA)','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331182,'11 The Artificial Intelligence Act','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331183,'13 The European Cyber Defence Policy','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331184,'15 GDPR','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331185,'16 The EU Economic Security Strategy','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331186,'17 EU- Indo-Pasific Stratgy','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331187,'18 The EU-China Relations','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331188,'19 EU -ASEAN Relations','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331189,'20 The New Pact on Migration and Asylum','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331190,'21 The NIS 2 Directive','2025-10-21 13:17:14'),(331191,'Green deal, innovation focus related to Agtech','2025-10-21 13:17:15'),(331192,'---','2025-10-21 13:17:15'),(331193,'the key influencing activity is targeted at startup, innovation and research commissioner of EU commission We would like to present how important it is to have such actions and VC environment supported by EU commission, especially for companies coming from smaller countries like Slovenia, where there is a lack of domestic market and domestic funding opportunities Another topic we plan to emphasize is the importance of connecting different technologies, where EU already has very significant role/leading global position like connecting automated digital insect monitoring and biological crop protection Such connection should be done through infrastructural projects (similar to what was done with weather station and we now all benefit from much better weather data and forecast) The need for such top-down approach is mainly die to fragmentation of EU farms that can not afford to build digital insect monitoring infrastructure that would benefit all stakeholders','2025-10-21 13:17:15'),(331194,'EU Framework Decisions: CEP, through its activities and communication channels, strongly promotes and supports the implementation of the relevant EU instruments, develops country-specific information (Probation in Europe), exchanges knowledge on practical examples, identifies possible ways for improvements and provides for practical recommendations, supports for training and raises awareness','2025-10-21 13:17:16'),(331195,'Alternatives to (Pre-trial) Detention: CEP works with its members, partners and the EC to support implementation of alternatives to (pre-trial) detention and further advocate for probation services to take on a more important role in ensuring that through the supervision, guidance and assistance, the individual rights of those concerned and the community safety considerations are properly balanced CEP delivers a specific activities and addresses the topic across its work programme','2025-10-21 13:17:16'),(331196,'Violent Extremism: Violent extremism and radicalization in the EU are paramount concerns for EC and CEP CEP pursues co-operation with bodies in counter terrorism including the EU Knowledge Hub for Prevention of Radicalisation (former RAN) for better co-ordination and joint-working, bringing in probation bodies and practitioners CEP organises specific activities and works with partners to raise awareness and disseminate knowledge about best practices via its website, newsletters & media','2025-10-21 13:17:16'),(331197,'Education & Training: CEP is active in the field of Education & Training for probation staff, both initial (basic) training as continuous training updates and possibilities to learn skills during the working period CEP has set up a Europe wide active network of education professionals to exchange experience and best practices between countries and bodies in the field of education and training to share knowledge updates in relation to legislative developments, intervention Guidelines from the European Commission and the Council of Europe and other research findings to have an information data base and central resource point on innovation and good practices presented at CEP expert network and other meetings on the CEP website','2025-10-21 13:17:16'),(331198,'Gender-based Violence: CEP aims to increase awareness of gender-based violence in probation and address gender inequality, especially towards women and girls, focusing on sexual abuse and domestic violence CEP promotes the exchange of knowledge and good practices, disseminates information on the Istanbul convention, the Council of Europe Convention on preventing and combating violence against women and domestic violence (CETS No210)','2025-10-21 13:17:16'),(331199,'Mental Health: The prevalence of various mental health issues among probationers is considerably higher than in the community CEP aims to share experience and good practices between CEP members, experts on mental health in probation, in order to improve programs, interventions and ways of working with people under probations suffering mental health problems','2025-10-21 13:17:16'),(331200,'V rámci naší činnosti se zaměřujeme zejména na oblast zdravotnictví Společnosti v holdingu AKESO jsou zejména poskytovatelé zdravotních služeb Dále se zaměřujeme na rozvojovou spolupráci v oblasti zdravotnictví, pharma a biotechnologií, a to jak z pohledu běžného provozu, tak v oblasti výzkumu a vývoje','2025-10-21 13:17:16'),(331201,'Klíčová témata, která chceme řešit jsou možnosti rozvojové spolupráce, zejména v oblasti zdravotnictví a dále možné podpory investic, či rozvojové spolupráce v této oblasti','2025-10-21 13:17:16'),(331202,'Alle für die regionale Wirtschaft relevanten EU-Initiativen, EU-Strategien und EU-Rechtssetzungsverfahren auf folgenden Gebieten:','2025-10-21 13:17:17'),(331203,'- Auswirkungen des Russland-Krieges in der Ukraine auf die bayerische Wirtschaft, insbes mit Blick auf Energiethemen, internationalen Handel und geopolitische Umbrüche','2025-10-21 13:17:17'),(331204,'- Vollendung bzw Verbesserung von zentralen Themen für den EU-Binnenmarkt für KMUs, insbes für KMUs im Rahmen von Entbürokratisierung und Simplifizierung / Vereinfachungen von Gesetzgebungsverfahren (Omnibus-Strategie der EU-KOM)','2025-10-21 13:17:17'),(331205,'- EU Green Deal Themen CSR/Nachhaltigkeit, Digitalisierung und Resilienz: s u','2025-10-21 13:17:17'),(331206,'- COVID 19 - Wirtschaftshilfen der Bundesregierung/des Freistaats Bayern für Unternehmen in der Krise, Resilienzthematik, Quarantäne- und Hygienevorschriften, Grenz-/Einreisebestimmungen','2025-10-21 13:17:17'),(331207,'- Internationale Handelspolitik und Entwicklungspolitik','2025-10-21 13:17:17'),(331208,'- Außenwirtschaftsförderung auf europäischer Ebene','2025-10-21 13:17:17'),(331209,'- Post-Brexit W