g defence funding','2025-10-21 13:17:23'),(331266,'- Trade agreements and trade defence instruments','2025-10-21 13:17:23'),(331267,'- EU Single Market Strategy','2025-10-21 13:17:23'),(331268,'- Promoting Finland\'s connectivity','2025-10-21 13:17:23'),(331269,'- Support and reconstruction of Ukraine','2025-10-21 13:17:23'),(331270,'Solvency II, ATA, IDD, International Insurance Programmes, OECD-Beps papers, permanent EIOPA contact, All for Captives relevant EC Directives and regulation','2025-10-21 13:17:29'),(331271,'We represent interests of the voluntary and community sector in Northern Ireland Our activities target EU legislation regarding employment, equality, economic development and social development','2025-10-21 13:17:29'),(331272,'Particular interest in EU Special Committee in the implementation of The Windsor Framework','2025-10-21 13:17:29'),(331273,'Seeking to influence EU institutions\' understanding of and approach to the unique post-Brexit circumstances on the island of Ireland, most particularly with regard to the implementation of the Windsor Framework The influence activities are intended to ensure that where the activities of these institutions have a direct or indirect impact on Northern Ireland (eg through the Windsor Framework) that the relevant officials are informed of the experience and perception of key stakeholders in the community and voluntary sector Northern Ireland','2025-10-21 13:17:29'),(331274,'GOTS has an interest in EU activities – initiatives, policies and legislative files – concerning the use of the term organic in relation to textiles Specifically, relevant standards and criteria for organic fibre, organic textiles, public procurement (including green public procurement), textiles and apparel, and policy developments concerning these','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331275,'The key legislation that GOTS follows:','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331276,'Directive (EU) 2025/794 (Stop the Clock Directive)','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331277,'Proposed Omnibus Regulation','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331278,'Proposed Directive (EU) on amending Directive 2008/98/EC on waste (Waste Framework Directive)','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331279,'Regulation (EU) 2025/40 on packaging and packaging waste','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331280,'Regulation (EU) 2024/1781 on ecodesign for sustainable products','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331281,'Directive (EU) 2024/1760 on corporate sustainability due diligence (CSDDD)','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331282,'Directive (EU) 2024/825 on empowering consumers for the green transition','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331283,'Proposed Directive (EU) 2023/0085 (COD) on green claims','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331284,'Directive (EU) 2022/2464 on corporate sustainability reporting (CSRD)','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331285,'Directive (EU) 2014/24 on public procurement','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331286,'Regulation (EU) 2011/1007 on textile fibre names and related labelling and marking of the fibre composition of textile products','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331287,'Regulation (EU) 2010/66 on EU Ecolabel','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331288,'Regulation (EU) 2006/1907 on Registration, Evaluation, Authorisation and Registration of Chemicals (REACH)','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331289,'EU Strategy for Sustainable and Circular Textiles','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331290,'Product Environmental Footprint (PEF), Category Rules for Apparel and Footwear','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331291,'Evaluation of Public Procurement Directives','2025-10-21 13:17:30'),(331292,'Ogni iniziativa legislativa attinente alla tutela delle opere dell\'ingegno, alla gestione collettiva del diritto d\'autore e al settore culturale','2025-10-21 13:17:31'),(331293,'Regulation (EU) 2019/1009 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 5 June 2019 laying down rules on the making available on the market of EU fertilising products and amending Regulations (EC) No 1069/2009 and (EC) No 1107/2009 and repealing Regulation (EC) No 2003/2003','2025-10-21 13:17:32'),(331294,'VITO as a responsible Research and Technology Organisation addressing the EU and global societal challenges seeks to increase its impact by advocating and acting on EU policies','2025-10-21 13:17:33'),(331295,'VITO’s main thematic policy areas:','2025-10-21 13:17:33'),(331296,'A regenerative economy: economy and ecology in balance – we aim to drive economic prosperity through te sustainable use of resources while reinforcing planetary boundaries','2025-10-21 13:17:33'),(331297,'Resilient ecosystems: we help companies and governments with climate mitigation and adaptation solutions We aim to create ecosystems that are more resilient to disasters, thereby enhancing our overall resilience and security','2025-10-21 13:17:33'),(331298,'A healthy living environment: a healthy and sustainable living environment for all is a core element of VITO’s vision Here, we focus on how to maintain a harmonious balance between the human environment, nature, agriculture and industry','2025-10-21 13:17:33'),(331299,'Net Stable Funding Ratio (NSFR)','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331300,'EU-Handelspolitik','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331301,'Verantwortungsvolle Beschaffung','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331302,'Europäisches Lieferkettengesetz','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331303,'Europäischer Grüner Deal','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331304,'EU-Aktionsplan zur Kreislaufwirtschaft','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331305,'EU-Wasserstoffstrategie','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331306,'EU-Stoffpolitik','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331307,'As an international aircraft lessor with a presence in Ireland, our organisation monitors EU legislative and policy developments that may have a material impact on the aircraft leasing industry While we are not currently engaged in direct advocacy activities, we would like to retain the ability to provide feedback or engage in dialogue with EU institutions or relevant stakeholders should the need arise','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331308,'In particular, we are interested in the following areas relevant to our industry:','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331309,'•	Sanctions-related regulations and directives, especially those relating to restrictions on leasing or exporting aircraft, insurance recoveries and prohibitions on the provision of technical or financial services This includes ongoing developments under Council Regulations (EU) No 269/2014 and 833/2014, as well as related implementing decisions','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331310,'•	Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) regulations, with a focus on initiatives affecting aircraft emissions, carbon reporting, sustainable finance (eg, the EU Taxonomy Regulation), and corporate disclosure requirements under the Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive (CSRD) As ESG-related compliance expectations grow, we are interested in understanding and potentially contributing to how such rules apply in the context of aircraft leasing','2025-10-21 13:17:34'),(331311,'•	Consistent with our focus on ESG matters, employment matters are of interest to us as an organisation with operations in Ireland','2025-10-21 13:17:35'),(331312,'•	Tariff policies and trade-related measures, particularly those that may impact the cross-border movement of aircraft, aviation parts, or related services We monitor developments related to customs duties, import restrictions, and trade retaliation measures that could affect leasing operations across the EU and other applicable jurisdictions','2025-10-21 13:17:35'),(331313,'1 Participación en conferencias y reuniones de la ECAC, European Civil Aviation Conference','2025-10-21 13:17:35'),(331314,'Prudential requirements Fintech Sustainable Finance Circular economy, Banking Recovery and Resolution EBA consultations  Banking UnionVehicle taxation, Directive 2015/413 - Facilitation of cross-border exchange of information on road-safety-related traffic offences, Motor vehicle block exemption regulation, PSD2, GDPR, AML','2025-10-21 13:17:36'),(331315,'Textes législatifs en lien avec la mise en oeuvre du Pacte vert (règ