 related to project application procedures within the frameworks of official EU funding platforms (such as WBIF, WeBalkans, or InvestEU)','2025-10-21 13:18:39'),(331563,'Registration is pursued in good faith to enhance transparency regarding our participation in EU-funded mechanisms, and to ensure eligibility in calls that reference or encourage voluntary registration We acknowledge that the Transparency Register is not intended for general project applicants or operational beneficiaries, and we submit this registration with the understanding that our participation is limited to publicly accessible funding channels without any intention to influence EU policymaking','2025-10-21 13:18:39'),(331564,'There are various policies of interested such as: CountEmissionsEU, Digital Service Act, Cross border workers','2025-10-21 13:18:40'),(331565,'European Eletronic Communications Code Roaming Regulation State aid guidelines for next generation networks Gigabit Infrastructure Act','2025-10-21 13:18:41'),(331566,'- Leyes y directivas relativas a la Inteligencia Artificial, como EU Artificial Intelligence Act','2025-10-21 13:18:42'),(331567,'Politiques européennes de protection des consommateurs dans le cadre d’un voyage dont les divers règlements sur les droits des passagers et la directive sur les voyages à forfait','2025-10-21 13:18:42'),(331568,'Le réseau est particulièrement attentif aux réglementations nationales et européennes relatives aux sujets suivants :','2025-10-21 13:18:42'),(331569,'- protection des consommateurs et droits des passagers','2025-10-21 13:18:42'),(331570,'- responsabilité des professionnels du tourisme dans le cadre de voyages à forfait','2025-10-21 13:18:42'),(331571,'- égalité de traitement des acteurs économiques','2025-10-21 13:18:42'),(331572,'Industrial Deal, ETS, CBAM','2025-10-21 13:18:43'),(331573,'Competition policy, Competitiveness','2025-10-21 13:18:43'),(331574,'Sustainable reporting','2025-10-21 13:18:43'),(331575,'Trade policy,','2025-10-21 13:18:43'),(331576,'Internal market policy','2025-10-21 13:18:43'),(331577,'General-Purpose AI Code of Practice (Working Groups)/ EU AI Office - European Commission','2025-10-21 13:18:45'),(331578,'VNO-NCW is in Brussel in principe actief op alle onderwerpen op sociaal en economisch gebied die van belang kunnen zijn voor het Nederlandse bedrijfsleven De verantwoordelijkheden binnen het kantoor Brussel van VNO-NCW zijn te vinden op de website van VNO-NCW,','2025-10-21 13:18:46'),(331579,'http://wwwvno-ncwnl/over_vnoncw/KantoorBrussel/Pages/defaultaspx','2025-10-21 13:18:46'),(331580,'De specifieke onderwerpen waar VNO-NCW mee bezig is zijn:','2025-10-21 13:18:46'),(331581,'- interne markt strategie: COM(2015) 550 final','2025-10-21 13:18:46'),(331582,'- digital single market: COM(2015) 192 final','2025-10-21 13:18:46'),(331583,'(Digital Single Market mid-term review: COM(2017)     228 final)','2025-10-21 13:18:46'),(331584,'- Mobiliteitspakket: COM(2017) 283 final','2025-10-21 13:18:46'),(331585,'- (herziening) detacheringsrichtlijn: COM(2016)128','2025-10-21 13:18:46'),(331586,'- CMU: COM(2015) 468 final','2025-10-21 13:18:46'),(331587,'(Mid-term review CMU: COM(2017) 292 final)','2025-10-21 13:18:46'),(331588,'- mededeling handelspolitiek: COM(2010)343 final','2025-10-21 13:18:46'),(331589,'Tobacco Products Directive Revision (TPD 3)','2025-10-21 13:18:50'),(331590,'Directive on Tobacco and Tobacco-related products Excise Duties (TAXUD)','2025-10-21 13:18:50'),(331591,'Cardiovascular Health Plan','2025-10-21 13:18:50'),(331592,'6-Month-Standstill after product registration','2025-10-21 13:18:50'),(331593,'Mighty Earth has been, continues to be, or intends to be engaged in conversations with various EU institutions and officials in relation to the following legislative measures, policy initiatives and dialogues:','2025-10-21 13:18:50'),(331594,'EU Sustainable Corporate Due Diligence Directive (CSDDD)','2025-10-21 13:18:50'),(331595,'EU Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive (CSRD)','2025-10-21 13:18:50'),(331596,'As a not-for-profit campaigning organisation, Mighty Earth conducts various types of communications, including public communications (through the traditional media, public polling, open letters, social media channels and our website), supporter communications (eg via email), targeted communications to specific audiences (eg webinars and policy briefings for expert audiences and EU officials), and individual communications with specific Commission officials, member state permanent representations, and elected European Parliamentarians and their offices','2025-10-21 13:18:50'),(331597,'Most of our communications with EU institutions are directed towards DG Environment at the Commission, staff at permanent representations with responsibility for files related to the legislative and policy initiatives listed above, and members of the European Parliament’s environment committee (Envi) However, we have also communicated with Parliamentary representatives on Legal Affairs (JURI), and may at times also communicate officials dealing with agricultural and climate policy, as well as international partnerships','2025-10-21 13:18:50'),(331598,'Mighty Earth is a regular participant in the Deforestation Platform meetings hosted monthly by EC’s DG Environment','2025-10-21 13:18:50'),(331599,'Elektronisk kommunikation och närliggande områden som säkerhet och handel','2025-10-21 13:18:51'),(331600,'The Directive on security of network and information systems (NIS Directive)','2025-10-21 13:18:51'),(331601,'Legislative and non-legislative initiatives related to the EU digital agenda, as well as educational and cultural initiatives to promote the audio sector and streaming In particular, any initiatives relating to competition (eg DMA), copyright, platform regulation, content regulation, media and audiovisual regulation','2025-10-21 13:18:52'),(331602,'The ACM Europe Technology Policy Committee (Europe TPC), an arm of ACM\'s