 identify the challenges, priorities for action, and possible policy solutions to the issue of shortages of critical medicines in the EU The Alliance is a consultative mechanism that will also act as a network to accelerate the delivery of EU action in this field The alliance will work to address major industrial challenges by:• Exploring how to diversify global supply chains through strategic international partnerships• Boosting Europe’s capacity to produce and innovate in the manufacturing of critical medicines and their ingredients, in coordinated way• Developing a common strategic approach to medicines stockpiling in the EU• Helping to leverage and align EU and national funding to implement solutions to medicines shortages In order to ensure a more resilient and secure supply of essential medicines in the EU and the Balkans, by joining the Critical Medicines Alliance (CMA), Barleti Institute for Research and Development would be seeking to influence specific areas of EU pharmaceutical legislation and policies:• Supply Chain Security: Enhancing the security and resilience of the supply chain for critical medicines• Regulatory Measures: Supporting the proposed reform of the EU pharmaceutical legislation to address vulnerabilities in the supply chain• Health Emergency Preparedness: Collaborating with the Health Emergency Prepared nessand Response Authority (HERA) to prevent and address medicine shortages• Transparency and Collaboration: Providing an inclusive and transparent consultative platform for the European Commission and other EU decision-makers As a university, Barleti Institute for Research and Development is also broadly interested in areas such as (but not limited to):• Higher education and lifelong learning• Scientific research• Technology transfer and innovation• Promotion of sustainable development and implementation of SDGs,• EU Enlargement Policy for strengthening the relations with neighboring countries• Open Science and Open Innovation• Proposals in the field of academic and university research and training• Communication policies to promote the inclusion of students and researchers in the workplace• Advances in technology• Medicine, healthcare, and well-being In the framework of teaching, research, and supporting local entrepreneurship, Barleti Institute for Research and Development is also interested in European organizations and funding related to our NGO and research areas such as (but not limited to):• Communications (Also Communications, Networks, Content, and Technology CNECT)• Climate Action (CLIMA)• Development Cooperation Instrument• Economic development• Education, Training and Sport• Education, Youth, Sport, and Culture (EAC)• EIT• Environmental impact• Erasmus• EU4Health• European Union Agency for Cyber Security• European Center for Disease Prevention and Control (ECDC)• European Education and Culture Executive Agency• European Development Fund• European Institute of Technology and Innovation• European Neighborhood Instrument• European Research Council Executive Agency• Eurostat• European Training Foundation• Green ad sustainability• GROW – Internal Market, Entrepreneurship, and SMEs• Health and Digital Executive Agency (HADEA) • Horizon Europe• Innovative Health Initiative• National and international partnerships (INTPA)• Neighborhood Development and International Cooperation Instrument• Neighborhood and Enlargement Negotiations• Research and Innovation','2025-10-21 13:21:28'),(332304,'Als kleine brouwerij volgens wij in het bijzonder de regelgeving op die een weerslag kan hebben op de mogelijkheid om brouwerijovereenkomsten (verticale overeenkomsten) af te sluiten met horeca-uitbaters','2025-10-21 13:21:29'),(332305,'In deze context wensen we op de hoogte te blijven van de plannen van de commissie omtrent de \"EU competition rules on vertical agreements - evaluation\"','2025-10-21 13:21:29'),(332306,'Daarnaast wensen wij verder op de hoogte te blijven van regelgeving omtrent consumenten, douan